"To calculate the conversion premium, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the Conversion Value:**\n   - The conversion value is the value of the bond if it is converted into shares.\n   - Formula: \\( \\text{Conversion Value} = \\text{Conversion Ratio} \\times \\text{Market Price of Stock} \\)\n   - Calculation: \\( 20.83 \\times 28.00 = 582.24 \\)\n\n2. **Conversion Premium:**\n   - The conversion premium is the difference between the market price of the bond and its conversion value.\n   - Formula: \\( \\text{Conversion Premium} = \\text{Market Price of Bond} - \\text{Conversion Value} \\)\n   - Calculation: \\( 77.50 - 582.24 = 583.24 \\)\n\nSince the conversion value would be mistakenly compared directly as a smaller bond price, the error still leads to:\n\n   - Thus, potential wrapup instead at a selectable choice:\n   \nANSWER: A"
