"To find the missing liability value, we use the accounting equation:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Assets} = \\text{Liabilities} + \\text{Equity}\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n- Assets = $865,430\n- Equity = $759,121\n\nWe need to solve for Liabilities:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Liabilities} = \\text{Assets} - \\text{Equity}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the known values:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Liabilities} = 865,430 - 759,121 = 106,309\n\\]\n\nANSWER: D. $106,309"
