"To calculate the price of a zero-coupon U.S. Treasury note with 4 years to maturity, we use the spot rate for 4 years.\n\nThe relevant spot rate given in the table is 7.16%.\n\nThe formula to calculate the price of a zero-coupon bond is:\n\n\\[ \\text{Price} = \\frac{\\text{Face Value}}{(1 + \\text{Spot Rate})^{\\text{Years to Maturity}}} \\]\n\nAssuming a face value of $1,000, the price is calculated as follows:\n\n\\[ \\text{Price} = \\frac{1000}{(1 + 0.0716)^4} \\]\n\n\\[ \\text{Price} = \\frac{1000}{(1.0716)^4} \\]\n\n\\[ \\text{Price} = \\frac{1000}{1.315556} \\]\n\n\\[ \\text{Price} \\approx 760.62 \\]\n\nHowever, this calculated price isn't directly matching any of the given options, so I must have misunderstood or misreported the data. After recalculating, none of the provided options match the answer. I apologize, but usually, this would highlight a need to reexamine the question for any overlooked details.\n\nANSWER: A. $758.35."
"To calculate the new break-even point after the 8% price increase, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the new sales price per unit:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{New Sales Price} = \\text{Current Sales Price} \\times (1 + \\text{Price Increase})\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{New Sales Price} = 125 \\times 1.08 = 135\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the new contribution margin per unit:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{New Contribution Margin} = \\text{New Sales Price} - \\text{Variable Cost}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{New Contribution Margin} = 135 - 98 = 37\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the new break-even point in units:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Break-even Point (units)} = \\frac{\\text{Fixed Costs}}{\\text{New Contribution Margin}}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{Break-even Point (units)} = \\frac{23,000}{37} \\approx 621.62\n   \\]\n   Round up to the nearest whole unit: 622 units.\n\n4. **Calculate the new break-even point in dollars:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Break-even Point (dollars)} = \\text{Break-even Point (units)} \\times \\text{New Sales Price}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{Break-even Point (dollars)} = 622 \\times 135 = 83,970\n   \\]\n\nIt looks like there was a slight error in the rounding step. The closest option is:\n\nANSWER: B. 622 units and $83,915.98."
"To calculate the modified duration, we use the following formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Modified Duration} = \\frac{\\text{Macaulay Duration}}{1 + \\frac{\\text{Yield to Maturity}}{n}}\n\\]\n\nwhere:\n- Macaulay Duration = 10 years\n- Yield to Maturity (YTM) = 8% or 0.08\n- \\( n \\) is the number of compounding periods per year. Since it's not specified, we assume annual compounding, so \\( n = 1 \\).\n\nPlugging in the numbers:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Modified Duration} = \\frac{10}{1 + \\frac{0.08}{1}} = \\frac{10}{1.08} \\approx 9.26 \\text{ years}\n\\]\n\nThus, the correct choice is:\n\nANSWER: B."
"To determine the equity beta for each company, we need to account for the impact of debt using the Hamada equation:\n\n\\[ \\beta_{\\text{equity}} = \\beta_{\\text{unlevered}} \\times \\left(1 + \\left(1 - \\text{Tax Rate}\\right) \\times \\frac{\\text{Debt}}{\\text{Equity}}\\right) \\]\n\nGiven:\n- \\(\\beta_{\\text{unlevered}} = 1.10\\)\n- Tax Rate = 35%\n\n### North Pole Calculation:\n\n- Debt = $2,700,000\n- Equity = $3,900,000\n\n\\[ \\beta_{\\text{equity, North}} = 1.10 \\times \\left(1 + (1 - 0.35) \\times \\frac{2,700,000}{3,900,000}\\right) \\]\n\n\\[ \\beta_{\\text{equity, North}} = 1.10 \\times \\left(1 + 0.65 \\times 0.6923\\right) \\]\n\n\\[ \\beta_{\\text{equity, North}} = 1.10 \\times (1 + 0.45) \\]\n\n\\[ \\beta_{\\text{equity, North}} = 1.10 \\times 1.45 \\]\n\n\\[ \\beta_{\\text{equity, North}} = 1.60 \\]\n\n### South Pole Calculation:\n\n- Debt = $3,900,000\n- Equity = $2,700,000\n\n\\[ \\beta_{\\text{equity, South}} = 1.10 \\times \\left(1 + (1 - 0.35) \\times \\frac{3,900,000}{2,700,000}\\right) \\]\n\n\\[ \\beta_{\\text{equity, South}} = 1.10 \\times \\left(1 + 0.65 \\times 1.4444\\right) \\]\n\n\\[ \\beta_{\\text{equity, South}} = 1.10 \\times (1 + 0.939) \\]\n\n\\[ \\beta_{\\text{equity, South}} = 1.10 \\times 1.939 \\]\n\n\\[ \\beta_{\\text{equity, South}} = 2.13 \\]\n\nANSWER: B. North:1.60, South:2.13."
