"To find the accounting break-even level, we need to calculate the break-even point in terms of units sold where net income equals zero. The formula for the accounting break-even point is:\n\n\\[ Q = \\frac{FC + D}{P - V} \\]\n\nwhere:\n- \\( Q \\) is the break-even quantity.\n- \\( FC \\) is the fixed costs.\n- \\( D \\) is the depreciation.\n- \\( P \\) is the sales price per unit.\n- \\( V \\) is the variable cost per unit.\n\nGiven:\n- Fixed costs (\\( FC \\)) = $410,000\n- Depreciation (\\( D \\)) = $120,000\n- Sales price per abalone (\\( P \\)) = $39\n- Variable costs per abalone (\\( V \\)) = $7.15\n\nPlugging in the values:\n\n\\[ Q = \\frac{410,000 + 120,000}{39 - 7.15} \\]\n\nCalculate the denominator:\n\n\\[ 39 - 7.15 = 31.85 \\]\n\nNow, calculate \\( Q \\):\n\n\\[ Q = \\frac{530,000}{31.85} \\approx 16,640.5 \\]\n\nThus, the accounting break-even level is approximately 16,640.5 units.\n\nANSWER: A."
"To calculate the modified duration of the bond, we can use the following formula for approximate modified duration:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Modified Duration} \\approx \\frac{(P_{-} - P_{+})}{2 \\times P_0 \\times \\Delta y}\n\\]\n\nWhere:\n- \\( P_{-} \\) is the price if yields fall (100.71).\n- \\( P_{+} \\) is the price if yields rise (99.29).\n- \\( P_0 \\) is the original price of the bond (100 if at par).\n- \\( \\Delta y \\) is the change in yield in decimal form (0.001 for 10 basis points).\n\nPlugging in the numbers:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Modified Duration} \\approx \\frac{(100.71 - 99.29)}{2 \\times 100 \\times 0.001} \n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{Modified Duration} \\approx \\frac{1.42}{0.2} \n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{Modified Duration} \\approx 7.10\n\\]\n\nThus, the modified duration of the bond is approximately 7.10.\n\nANSWER: C."
