"To calculate the equivalent units for material costs using the weighted-average method, follow these steps:\n\n1. **For each quarter:**\n   - Calculate the ending work in process inventory.\n   - Determine equivalent units for materials.\n\nMaterials are added 50% at the beginning and 50% at the end of the process. Based on this, materials are fully added to started and transferred units.\n\n### Quarter 1:\n- **Started and Transferred Out:** 235,000 units\n- **Ending Work in Process (WIP):** 255,000 (Started) - 235,000 (Transferred) = 20,000 units\n\nEquivalent units (Materials) = Transferred Units + Ending WIP\n= 235,000 + 20,000 (100% complete for materials)\n= 255,000 units\n\n### Quarter 2:\n- **Started and Transferred Out:** 250,000 units\n- **Ending WIP:** 275,000 (Started) - 250,000 (Transferred) = 25,000 units\n\nEquivalent units (Materials) = Transferred Units + Ending WIP\n= 250,000 + 25,000 (100% complete for materials)\n= 275,000 units\n\n### Quarter 3:\n- **Started and Transferred Out:** 275,000 units\n- **Ending WIP:** 290,000 (Started) - 275,000 (Transferred) = 15,000 units\n\nEquivalent units (Materials) = Transferred Units + Ending WIP\n= 275,000 + 15,000 (100% complete for materials)\n= 290,000 units\n\n### Quarter 4:\n- **Started and Transferred Out:** 280,000 units\n- **Ending WIP:** 300,000 (Started) - 280,000 (Transferred) = 20,000 units\n\nEquivalent units (Materials) = Transferred Units + Ending WIP\n= 280,000 + 20,000 (100% complete for materials)\n= 300,000 units\n\n### Total Equivalent Units (All Quarters):\n255,000 + 275,000 + 290,000 + 300,000 = 1,120,000 units\n\nHowever, since we need the average per quarter:\n1,120,000 / 4 = 280,000 per quarter (independently, not averaged across quarters as a sum).\n\n### Checking Options:\nAnalyze the multiple-choice options and the values:\n- Options presented include units that total differently when listed: A. 293,250. B. 295,250. C. 296,900. D. 295,900.\n- The choice from calculations is based 