"To solve for the interest rate, we use the future value formula:\n\n\\[ FV = PV \\times (1 + r)^n \\]\n\nWhere:\n- \\( FV \\) is the future value.\n- \\( PV \\) is the present value.\n- \\( r \\) is the interest rate.\n- \\( n \\) is the number of years.\n\nRearranging the formula to solve for \\( r \\):\n\n\\[ r = \\left(\\frac{FV}{PV}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{n}} - 1 \\]\n\nLet's calculate for each set:\n\n1. **First row:**\n   - \\( PV = 242 \\), \\( FV = 345 \\), \\( n = 4 \\)\n   - \\( r = \\left(\\frac{345}{242}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{4}} - 1 \\approx 0.0969 \\text{ or } 9.69\\% \\)\n\n2. **Second row:**\n   - \\( PV = 410 \\), \\( FV = 927 \\), \\( n = 8 \\)\n   - \\( r = \\left(\\frac{927}{410}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{8}} - 1 \\approx 0.1065 \\text{ or } 10.65\\% \\)\n\n3. **Third row:**\n   - \\( PV = 51,700 \\), \\( FV = 152,184 \\), \\( n = 16 \\)\n   - \\( r = \\left(\\frac{152,184}{51,700}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{16}} - 1 \\approx 0.0703 \\text{ or } 7.03\\% \\)\n\n4. **Fourth row:**\n   - \\( PV = 18,750 \\), \\( FV = 538,600 \\), \\( n = 27 \\)\n   - \\( r = \\left(\\frac{538,600}{18,750}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{27}} - 1 \\approx 0.1301 \\text{ or } 13.01\\% \\)\n\nComparing these results with the options provided:\n\n- First row: 9.69% matches with Option C's 9.45% (closest)\n- Second row: 10.65% matches with Option C's 10.90% (closest)\n- Third row: 7.03% matches exactly with Option C's 7.03%\n- Fourth row: 13.01% matches with Option C's 13.51% (closest)\n\nANSWER: C"
"To calculate the U.S. dollar holding-period return using the recommended strategy, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Investment and Yield in Pesos:**\n   - Mexican 1-year bond yield: 6.5%.\n\n2. **Forward Exchange Rate:**\n   - Spot exchange rate: 9.5000 Pesos = U.S. $1.00.\n   - 1-year forward exchange rate: 9.8707 Pesos = U.S. $1.00.\n\n3. **Calculate the U.S. Dollar Equivalent Through Hedging:**\n   - Invest 1 peso in the Mexican bond; it grows to 1.065 pesos after one year.\n   - Hedge the foreign currency exposure using the forward rate.\n   - Convert the matured amount (1.065 pesos) to U.S. dollars at the forward rate:\n     \\[\n     \\text{U.S. Dollar Amount} = \\frac{1.065}{9.8707} = 0.1079 \\text{ U.S. dollars per peso}\n     \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the U.S. Dollar Return:**\n   - Initial U.S. dollar equivalent of 1 peso is \\( \\frac{1}{9.5000} = 0.1053 \\text{ U.S. dollars} \\).\n   - Holding-period return in U.S. dollars:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Return} = \\frac{0.1079 - 0.1053}{0.1053} = 0.0247 \\text{ or } 2.47\\%\n     \\]\n\nSince 2.47% closely aligns with the rounded figure and one of the options,\n\nANSWER: B. 2.50%."
"To find the missing value for Company 3, we need to use the Owners' Equity equation:\n\n\\[ \\text{Beginning Balance} + \\text{Net Income} - \\text{Net Loss} + \\text{Investments} - \\text{Distributions} = \\text{Ending Balance} \\]\n\nFor Company 3:\n\n- Beginning Balance = $0\n- Net Income = $0\n- Net Loss = ?\n- Investments = $150,000\n- Distributions = $0\n- Ending Balance = $101,400\n\nPlug these values into the equation:\n\n\\[ 0 + 0 - \\text{Net Loss} + 150,000 - 0 = 101,400 \\]\n\nSimplify the equation:\n\n\\[ 150,000 - \\text{Net Loss} = 101,400 \\]\n\nSolve for Net Loss:\n\n\\[ 150,000 - 101,400 = \\text{Net Loss} \\]\n\n\\[ \\text{Net Loss} = 48,600 \\]\n\nTherefore, the missing Net Loss value for Company 3 is $48,600.\n\nANSWER: C"
