"To calculate the mean and standard deviation of the Holding Period Returns (HPR) on stocks, we use the probabilities and corresponding HPRs given.\n\n### Mean (Expected HPR)\nThe mean HPR is calculated by multiplying each HPR by its probability and summing the results.\n\n\\[\n\\text{Mean HPR} = (0.35 \\times 44.5\\%) + (0.30 \\times 14.0\\%) + (0.35 \\times -16.5\\%)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{Mean HPR} = (0.35 \\times 44.5) + (0.30 \\times 14.0) + (0.35 \\times -16.5)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{Mean HPR} = 15.575 + 4.2 - 5.775 = 14.0\\%\n\\]\n\n### Standard Deviation\n1. Calculate the variance using the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Variance} = (0.35 \\times (44.5 - 14.0)^2) + (0.30 \\times (14.0 - 14.0)^2) + (0.35 \\times (-16.5 - 14.0)^2)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= (0.35 \\times 30.5^2) + (0.30 \\times 0^2) + (0.35 \\times -30.5^2)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= (0.35 \\times 930.25) + 0 + (0.35 \\times 930.25)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= 325.5875 + 0 + 325.5875 = 651.175\n\\]\n\n2. The standard deviation is the square root of the variance:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Standard Deviation} = \\sqrt{651.175} \\approx 25.52\\%\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the mean and standard deviation are 14% and 25.52%, respectively.\n\nANSWER: B."
"To calculate the theoretical price for a 6-month Japanese yen/U.S. dollar currency futures contract, we use the interest rate parity formula:\n\n\\[\nF = S \\times \\left( \\frac{1 + i_d}{1 + i_f} \\right)\n\\]\n\nWhere:\n- \\( F \\) is the forward exchange rate (futures price).\n- \\( S \\) is the spot exchange rate.\n- \\( i_d \\) is the domestic interest rate (U.S.).\n- \\( i_f \\) is the foreign interest rate (Japan).\n\nGiven data:\n- Spot exchange rate \\( S = 124.30 \\) JPY/USD\n- Japanese 6-month interest rate \\( i_f = 0.10\\% = 0.001 \\)\n- U.S. 6-month interest rate \\( i_d = 3.80\\% = 0.038 \\)\n\nSubstitute these values into the formula. Since it's a 6-month period, use half of the annual interest rate for each:\n\n\\[\nF = 124.30 \\times \\left( \\frac{1 + 0.038/2}{1 + 0.001/2} \\right)\n\\]\n\nCalculate the interest rate factors:\n\n- \\( 1 + i_d/2 = 1 + 0.038/2 = 1.019 \\)\n\n- \\( 1 + i_f/2 = 1 + 0.001/2 = 1.0005 \\)\n\nNow plug these into the formula:\n\n\\[\nF = 124.30 \\times \\left( \\frac{1.019}{1.0005} \\right)\n\\]\n\n\\[\nF = 124.30 \\times 1.01897951 \\approx 126.97346\n\\]\n\nANSWER: C."
