"To calculate the rate of return after incentive fees for an investor in the fund of funds, follow these steps:\n\n### Initial Returns Before Incentive Fees\n- Hedge Fund 1: $100 million * 20% = $20 million\n- Hedge Fund 2: $100 million * 10% = $10 million\n- Hedge Fund 3: $100 million * 30% = $30 million\n\nTotal gross return for all funds = $20m + $10m + $30m = $60 million\n\n### Incentive Fees for Each Fund\n- Hedge Fund 1 Incentive Fee: 20% of $20 million = $4 million\n- Hedge Fund 2 Incentive Fee: 20% of $10 million = $2 million\n- Hedge Fund 3 Incentive Fee: 20% of $30 million = $6 million\n\nTotal incentive fees for individual funds = $4m + $2m + $6m = $12 million\n\n### Net Returns for Each Fund\n- Hedge Fund 1 Net Return: $20 million - $4 million = $16 million\n- Hedge Fund 2 Net Return: $10 million - $2 million = $8 million\n- Hedge Fund 3 Net Return: $30 million - $6 million = $24 million\n\nTotal net return for all funds = $16m + $8m + $24m = $48 million\n\n### Fund of Funds Incentive Fee\n- Fund of Funds Gross Return: $48 million\n- Fund of Funds Incentive Fee: 20% of $48 million = $9.6 million\n\n### Net Return for Fund of Funds\nNet return = $48 million - $9.6 million = $38.4 million\n\n### Total Initial Investment\nTotal initial investment = $100 million * 3 = $300 million\n\n### Rate of Return for Fund of Funds\nRate of return = ($38.4 million / $300 million) * 100% = 12.8%\n\nANSWER: C"
