"To calculate the operating cycle, we need to determine the Inventory Period and the Accounts Receivable Period.\n\n**1. Inventory Period**:\n\\[\n\\text{Inventory Period} = \\frac{\\text{Average Inventory}}{\\text{Cost of Goods Sold per Day}}\n\\]\n\nAverage Inventory = \\(\\frac{\\text{Beginning Inventory} + \\text{Ending Inventory}}{2} = \\frac{17385 + 19108}{2} = 18246.5\\)\n\nCost of Goods Sold per Day = \\(\\frac{\\text{Cost of Goods Sold}}{365} = \\frac{165763}{365} = 454\\)\n\nInventory Period = \\(\\frac{18246.5}{454} = 40.21 \\, \\text{days}\\)\n\n**2. Accounts Receivable Period**:\n\\[\n\\text{Accounts Receivable Period} = \\frac{\\text{Average Accounts Receivable}}{\\text{Net Sales per Day}}\n\\]\n\nAverage Accounts Receivable = \\(\\frac{\\text{Beginning Accounts Receivable} + \\text{Ending Accounts Receivable}}{2} = \\frac{13182 + 13973}{2} = 13577.5\\)\n\nNet Sales per Day = \\(\\frac{\\text{Net Sales}}{365} = \\frac{216384}{365} = 593\\)\n\nAccounts Receivable Period = \\(\\frac{13577.5}{593} = 22.87 \\, \\text{days}\\)\n\n**3. Operating Cycle**: \n\\[\n\\text{Operating Cycle} = \\text{Inventory Period} + \\text{Accounts Receivable Period} = 40.21 + 22.87 = 63.08 \\, \\text{days}\n\\]\n\nANSWER: B"
