"To minimize the variance of a portfolio consisting of two assets, the weights \\( X_A \\) and \\( X_B \\) should be calculated using the following formulae:\n\nThe variance of the portfolio is given by:\n\\[\n\\sigma_p^2 = (X_A^2 \\cdot \\sigma_A^2) + (X_B^2 \\cdot \\sigma_B^2) + (2 \\cdot X_A \\cdot X_B \\cdot \\text{Cov}(A, B))\n\\]\n\nwhere:\n- \\(\\sigma_A = 33\\%\\) or 0.33\n- \\(\\sigma_B = 62\\%\\) or 0.62\n- \\(\\text{Cov}(A, B) = 0.001\\)\n\nThe weights should also satisfy: \n\\[ X_A + X_B = 1 \\]\n\\[ X_B = 1 - X_A \\]\n\nTo minimize the variance, we use the following formula derived based on the first order conditions:\n\\[ X_A = \\frac{\\sigma_B^2 - \\text{Cov}(A, B)}{\\sigma_A^2 + \\sigma_B^2 - 2 \\cdot \\text{Cov}(A, B)} \\]\n\nSubstituting the given values:\n- \\(\\sigma_A^2 = 0.33^2 = 0.1089\\)\n- \\(\\sigma_B^2 = 0.62^2 = 0.3844\\)\n\n\\[ X_A = \\frac{0.3844 - 0.001}{0.1089 + 0.3844 - 2 \\cdot 0.001} \\]\n\n\\[ X_A = \\frac{0.3834}{0.4923} \\]\n\nCalculating the above expression gives:\n\\[ X_A \\approx 0.7804 \\]\n\nThus, the weight \\( X_A \\) such that the variance of the portfolio is minimized is approximately 0.7804, matching option A.\n\nANSWER: A"
