"To find the break-even point, we need to calculate the contribution margin per unit and then use it to find the break-even point in units and dollars.\n\n1. **Calculate the Contribution Margin per Unit:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\text{Contribution Margin per Unit} = \\text{Sales Price per Unit} - \\text{Variable Costs per Unit}\n   \\]\n   \n   \\[\n   \\text{Contribution Margin per Unit} = 150 - 80 = 70\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the Break-even Point in Units:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\text{Break-even Point (units)} = \\frac{\\text{Fixed Expenses}}{\\text{Contribution Margin per Unit}}\n   \\]\n\n   \\[\n   \\text{Break-even Point (units)} = \\frac{42,000}{70} = 600\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the Break-even Point in Dollar Sales:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\text{Break-even Point (dollars)} = \\text{Break-even Point (units)} \\times \\text{Sales Price per Unit}\n   \\]\n\n   \\[\n   \\text{Break-even Point (dollars)} = 600 \\times 150 = 90,000\n   \\]\n\nSince the given options are close to 90,000, consider the closest option.\n\nANSWER: D. 600 units and $90,993.57."
