"To find the most probable value using the method of repetition, we calculate the weighted average of the observed angles. Each angle is weighted by the number of measurements:\n\n1. Convert all angle measurements to the same unit (seconds).\n   - \\(40^\\circ 20' = 40 \\times 3600 + 20 \\times 60 = 145200\\) seconds\n   - \\(40^\\circ 30' = 40 \\times 3600 + 30 \\times 60 = 145800\\) seconds\n   - \\(40^\\circ 45' = 40 \\times 3600 + 45 \\times 60 = 146700\\) seconds\n\n2. Multiply each angle by the number of measurements:\n   - Observer 1: \\(145200 \\times 2 = 290400\\)\n   - Observer 2: \\(145800 \\times 3 = 437400\\)\n   - Observer 3: \\(146700 \\times 4 = 586800\\)\n\n3. Add the results:\n   - Total sum = \\(290400 + 437400 + 586800 = 1314600\\)\n\n4. Total number of measurements:\n   - \\(2 + 3 + 4 = 9\\)\n\n5. Calculate the weighted average:\n   - \\(\\frac{1314600}{9} = 146066.67\\) seconds\n\n6. Convert back to degrees, minutes, and seconds:\n   - \\(146066.67\\) seconds\n   - \\(146066.67 \\div 3600 = 40\\) degrees\n   - Remainder: \\(146066.67 - 40 \\times 3600 = 66.67\\) seconds\n   - \\(66.67 \\div 60 = 1.1112\\)\n   - Minutes: \\(1\\)\n   - Seconds: \\(66.67 - 1 \\times 60 = 6.67\\)\n\nFinal angle: \\(40^\\circ 36' 6.67''\\)\n\nSince the problem provides options in a different format, we consider rounding:\n\nThe closest option is \\(40^\\circ 36' 26.67''\\).\n\nANSWER: B"
