"To calculate the horizontal distance from the slope distance and vertical angle, we use the formula:\n\n\\[ L_h = L_s \\times \\cos(\\theta) \\]\n\nwhere \\( L_h \\) is the horizontal distance, \\( L_s \\) is the slope distance, and \\(\\theta\\) is the vertical angle.\n\n### Calculation for \\( L_a \\):\n\n1. Slope distance (\\( L_s \\)) = 386.76 ft\n2. Vertical angle (\\(\\theta\\)) = \\( 5^\\circ 18' 00'' = 5 + \\frac{18}{60} = 5.3 \\) degrees\n\nConvert the angle to radians for calculation:\n\\[ \\theta \\text{ in radians} = 5.3 \\times \\frac{\\pi}{180} \\]\n\nCalculate the horizontal distance:\n\\[ L_{a} = 386.76 \\times \\cos(5.3 \\times \\frac{\\pi}{180}) \\]\n\\[ L_{a} \\approx 386.76 \\times 0.995 \\]\n\\[ L_{a} \\approx 384.11 \\text{ ft} \\]\n\n### Calculation for \\( L_b \\):\n\n1. Slope distance (\\( L_s \\)) = 2144.96 ft\n2. Vertical angle (\\(\\theta\\)) = \\(-4^\\circ 21' 20'' = -4.3555\\) degrees\n\nConvert the angle to radians:\n\\[ \\theta \\text{ in radians} = -4.3555 \\times \\frac{\\pi}{180} \\]\n\nCalculate the horizontal distance:\n\\[ L_{b} = 2144.96 \\times \\cos(-4.3555 \\times \\frac{\\pi}{180}) \\]\n\\[ L_{b} \\approx 2144.96 \\times 0.997 \\]\n\\[ L_{b} \\approx 2138.77 \\text{ ft} \\]\n\nBased on the calculations:\n\nANSWER: A. \\( L_{a} = 384.11 \\) ft, \\( L_{b} = 2138.77 \\) ft."
