"To determine the mode shares using the multinomial logit model, we will calculate the utility for each mode and then find their respective probabilities.\n\n### Step 1: Calculate Utility\n\nThe utility function is given by:\n\n\\[ U_k = A_k - 0.05T_a - 0.04T_w - 0.03T_r - 0.014C \\]\n\nFor **Private Auto**:\n- \\( T_a = 5 \\)\n- \\( T_w = 0 \\)\n- \\( T_r = 25 \\)\n- \\( C = 180 \\) (updated due to increase in fuel price)\n- \\( A_k = -0.01 \\)\n\n\\[ U_{\\text{auto}} = -0.01 - 0.05(5) - 0.04(0) - 0.03(25) - 0.014(180) \\]\n\\[ U_{\\text{auto}} = -0.01 - 0.25 - 0 - 0.75 - 2.52 \\]\n\\[ U_{\\text{auto}} = -3.53 \\]\n\nFor **Mass Transit**:\n- \\( T_a = 10 \\)\n- \\( T_w = 15 \\)\n- \\( T_r = 40 \\)\n- \\( C = 100 \\)\n- \\( A_k = -0.07 \\)\n\n\\[ U_{\\text{transit}} = -0.07 - 0.05(10) - 0.04(15) - 0.03(40) - 0.014(100) \\]\n\\[ U_{\\text{transit}} = -0.07 - 0.5 - 0.6 - 1.2 - 1.4 \\]\n\\[ U_{\\text{transit}} = -3.77 \\]\n\n### Step 2: Calculate Mode Shares\n\nThe probability of choosing a mode is given by the formula:\n\n\\[ P_k = \\frac{e^{U_k}}{e^{U_{\\text{auto}}} + e^{U_{\\text{transit}}}} \\]\n\n\\[ P_{\\text{auto}} = \\frac{e^{-3.53}}{e^{-3.53} + e^{-3.77}} \\]\n\\[ P_{\\text{auto}} \\approx \\frac{0.029}{0.029 + 0.023} \\]\n\\[ P_{\\text{auto}} \\approx \\frac{0.029}{0.052} \\]\n\\[ P_{\\text{auto}} \\approx 0.5577 \\text{ or } 55.77\\% \\]\n\n\\[ P_{\\text{transit}} = \\frac{e^{-3.77}}{e^{-3.53} + e^{-3.77}} \\]\n\\[ P_{\\text{transit}} \\approx \\frac{0.023}{0.052} \\]\n\\[ P_{\\text{transit}} \\approx 0.4423 \\text{ or } 44.23\\% \\]\n\nTherefore, the recalculated mode shares are:\n\n- \\( P_{\\text{auto}} \\approx 55.77\\% \\)\n- \\( P_{\\text{transit}} \\approx 44.23\\% \\)\n\n### Choice:\nThe closest percentage from the options given is:\n\nANSWER: C. Pauto=55,92% ;Pmass transit=44,08%."
"To solve the problem, we need to calculate the wind forces on the windward and leeward walls of the warehouse, and then sum them to get the total wind force.\n\n### Given Information:\n- Basic wind speed, \\( V = 40 \\, \\text{m/s} \\)\n- Wind exposure category = C\n- \\( K_d = 0.85 \\)\n- \\( K_{zt} = 1.0 \\)\n- \\( G = 0.85 \\)\n- \\( C_p = 0.8 \\) for windward wall, \\( C_p = -0.2 \\) for leeward wall\n- Dimensions: height \\( h = 9 \\, \\text{m} \\), width \\( w = 40 \\, \\text{m} \\)\n\n### Steps to Calculate Wind Force\n\n1. **Calculate the velocity pressure, \\( q_z \\):**\n   \\[ q_z = 0.613 \\cdot K_z \\cdot K_d \\cdot K_{zt} \\cdot V^2 \\]\n   For exposure category C and height 9 m, assume \\( K_z = 0.7 \\) (from Table 2.4, usually provided in references).\n\n   \\[ q_z = 0.613 \\cdot 0.7 \\cdot 0.85 \\cdot 1.0 \\cdot 40^2 \\]\n   \\[ q_z = 0.613 \\cdot 0.7 \\cdot 0.85 \\cdot 1600 \\]\n   \\[ q_z = 0.613 \\cdot 0.7 \\cdot 1360 \\]\n   \\[ q_z = 582.1 \\, \\text{N/m}^2 \\]\n\n2. **Calculate force on windward wall:**\n   \\[ F_{ww} = q_z \\cdot G \\cdot C_p \\cdot A \\]\n   \\[ A = \\text{width} \\times \\text{height} = 40 \\, \\text{m} \\times 9 \\, \\text{m} = 360 \\, \\text{m}^2 \\]\n   \\[ F_{ww} = 582.1 \\cdot 0.85 \\cdot 0.8 \\cdot 360 \\]\n   \\[ F_{ww} = 142,430 \\, \\text{N} \\]\n\n3. **Calculate force on leeward wall:**\n   \\[ F_{lw} = q_z \\cdot G \\cdot C_p \\cdot A \\]\n   \\[ F_{lw} = 582.1 \\cdot 0.85 \\cdot (-0.2) \\cdot 360 \\]\n   \\[ F_{lw} = -35,246 \\, \\text{N} \\]\n\n4. **Total wind force:**\n   \\[ F_{\\text{total}} = F_{ww} + F_{lw} \\]\n   \\[ F_{\\text{total}} = 142,430 - 35,246 \\]\n   \\[ F_{\\text{total}} = 107,184 \\, \\text{N} \\]\n\nThe options provided do not exactly match this calculated result. However, this indicates a possible error or misinterpretation in the given values, table references, or assumptions. \n\nAssuming an error in the provided selections and checking calculations could lead you to the provided correct