"To find the area of a polygon given its vertices, we can use the Shoelace Theorem (or Gauss's area formula). The formula is:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| \\sum_{i=1}^{n} (x_i y_{i+1} - y_i x_{i+1}) \\right|\n\\]\n\nFor the vertices \\( (x_1, y_1), (x_2, y_2), \\ldots, (x_n, y_n), (x_1, y_1) \\), where \\( n \\) is the number of vertices, and \\((x_{n+1}, y_{n+1}) = (x_1, y_1)\\) to close the polygon.\n\nGiven points for the polygon ABCDEA are:\n- \\( A(0, 0) \\)\n- \\( B(300, 100) \\)\n- \\( C(450, 350) \\)\n- \\( D(425, 600) \\)\n- \\( E(200, 600) \\)\n- \\( F(-100, 350) \\)\n\nLet's apply the Shoelace Theorem:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Area} &= \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 0 \\cdot 100 + 300 \\cdot 350 + 450 \\cdot 600 + 425 \\cdot 600 + 200 \\cdot 350 + (-100) \\cdot 0 \\right. \\\\\n&\\quad - \\left. (0 \\cdot 300 + 100 \\cdot 450 + 350 \\cdot 425 + 600 \\cdot 200 + 600 \\cdot (-100)) \\right|\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nCalculate each part:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n0 \\cdot 100 &= 0 \\\\\n300 \\cdot 350 &= 105000 \\\\\n450 \\cdot 600 &= 270000 \\\\\n425 \\cdot 600 &= 255000 \\\\\n200 \\cdot 350 &= 70000 \\\\\n(-100) \\cdot 0 &= 0 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n0 \\cdot 300 &= 0 \\\\\n100 \\cdot 450 &= 45000 \\\\\n350 \\cdot 425 &= 148750 \\\\\n600 \\cdot 200 &= 120000 \\\\\n600 \\cdot (-100) &= -60000 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nSum them up:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Sum 1} &= 0 + 105000 + 270000 + 255000 + 70000 + 0 = 700000 \\\\\n\\text{Sum 2} &= 0 + 45000 + 148750 + 120000 - 60000 = 253750 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nCalculate the area:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 700000 - 253750 \\right| = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 446250 = 223125\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area enclosed by the traverse ABCDEA is 223125 square units.\n\nANSWER: B"
"To find the total height of the transmission tower, we need to calculate the height above the instrument level (\\(h_1\\)) and the height below the instrument level (\\(h_2\\)) and then sum them.\n\n1. **Convert angles to decimal degrees:**\n   - \\(30^\\circ 42' = 30 + \\frac{42}{60} = 30.7^\\circ\\)\n   - \\(2^\\circ 30' = 2 + \\frac{30}{60} = 2.5^\\circ\\)\n\n2. **Calculate \\(h_1\\):**\n   - Use the tangent of the angle of elevation:\n   \\[\n   \\tan(30.7^\\circ) = \\frac{h_1}{200}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   h_1 = 200 \\times \\tan(30.7^\\circ) \\approx 118.67 \\, m\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate \\(h_2\\):**\n   - Use the tangent of the angle of depression:\n   \\[\n   \\tan(2.5^\\circ) = \\frac{h_2}{200}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   h_2 = 200 \\times \\tan(2.5^\\circ) \\approx 8.81 \\, m\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the total height \\(h\\):**\n   \\[\n   h = h_1 + h_2 = 118.67 + 8.81 = 127.48 \\, m\n   \\]\n\nThus, the total height of the transmission tower is approximately 127.482 m.\n\nANSWER: A"
