arification with correct calculations >>> \n   - Hence indeed after reconfirm careful options tally \n     - Fixed tally after any overlooked point >>> 772 cu yd choice translator \n\n5. **Double-check for correct choice:**\n   - Although slipped details might revise the yard metric, \n     with cross-examining round-off often leads toward right base > Most precision aligns: \"A. V =772.4 cu yd.\"\n\n**ANSWER: A. V =772.4 cu yd.**"
"To determine which stations have local attraction, we need to check if the difference between the fore bearing (F.B.) and back bearing (B.B.) of each line is exactly 180 degrees, which indicates no local attraction.\n\nLet's calculate for each line:\n\n1. **Line AB:**\n   - F.B. = 80\u00b045'\n   - B.B. = 260\u00b000'\n   - Difference = 260\u00b000' - 80\u00b045' = 179\u00b015'\n   - Deviation from 180\u00b0 = 0\u00b045' (indicates local attraction).\n\n2. **Line BC:**\n   - F.B. = 130\u00b030'\n   - B.B. = 311\u00b035'\n   - Difference = 311\u00b035' - 130\u00b030' = 181\u00b005'\n   - Deviation from 180\u00b0 = 1\u00b005' (indicates local attraction).\n\n3. **Line CD:**\n   - F.B. = 240\u00b015'\n   - B.B. = 60\u00b015'\n   - Adjusted B.B. = 240\u00b015' - 180\u00b0 = 60\u00b015'\n   - Difference = 240\u00b015' - 60\u00b015' = 180\u00b000'\n   - Deviation from 180\u00b0 = 0\u00b000' (no local attraction).\n\n4. **Line DA:**\n   - F.B. = 290\u00b030'\n   - B.B. = 110\u00b010'\n   - Adjusted B.B. = 290\u00b030' - 180\u00b0 = 110\u00b030'\n   - Difference = 290\u00b030' - 110\u00b010' = 180\u00b020'\n   - Deviation from 180\u00b0 = 0\u00b020' (indicates local attraction).\n\nFrom these calculations, only at station C and D do the differences match exactly 180\u00b0 or appropriately close to be negligible. The other stations show significant deviations from 180\u00b0 indicating local attraction.\n\nANSWER: B. Stations C and D are free from local attraction."
"To calculate the area between the chain line and the irregular boundary using the average ordinate rule, we follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the Intervals and Ordinates:**\n   - Intervals between chainages are 30 m.\n   - Ordinates (offsets) are: 0, 2.65, 3.80, 3.75, 4.65, 3.60, 5.00, 5.80.\n\n2. **Calculate the Average Ordinate:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Average Ordinate} = \\frac{\\text{Sum of Ordinates}}{\\text{Number of Ordinates}}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{Average Ordinate} = \\frac{0 + 2.65 + 3.80 + 3.75 + 4.65 + 3.60 + 5.00 + 5.80}{8}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{Average Ordinate} = \\frac{29.25}{8} = 3.65625\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the Area:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area} = \\text{Average Ordinate} \\times \\text{Length of the Base}\n   \\]\n   Length of the base = Total distance = 210 m.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area} = 3.65625 \\times 210 = 767.8125 \\text{ m}^2\n   \\]\n\n4. **Choose the Closest Option:**\n   The closest option to 767.8125 m\\(^2\\) is 767.825 m\\(^2\\).\n\nANSWER: C."
