"To adjust the geodetic quadrilateral, we need to ensure the sum of the angles matches the expected sum for a spherical quadrilateral. \n\nLet's calculate the actual sum of the given angles:\n- Angle 1: 29\u00b025'34\"\n- Angle 2: 58\u00b041'20\"\n- Angle 3: 69\u00b036'20\"\n- Angle 4: 22\u00b017'02\"\n- Angle 5: 30\u00b029'25\"\n- Angle 6: 57\u00b037'33\"\n- Angle 7: 50\u00b035'44\"\n- Angle 8: 41\u00b017'26\"\n\nAdd these angles to find their total sum:\n\n\\[ \\text{Sum} = 29^\\circ 25'34'' + 58^\\circ 41'20'' + 69^\\circ 36'20'' + 22^\\circ 17'02'' + 30^\\circ 29'25'' + 57^\\circ 37'33'' + 50^\\circ 35'44'' + 41^\\circ 17'26'' \\]\n\nConvert to seconds for easier addition:\n- Angle 1: \\( 29 \\times 3600 + 25 \\times 60 + 34 = 105334 \\) seconds\n- Angle 2: \\( 58 \\times 3600 + 41 \\times 60 + 20 = 211280 \\) seconds\n- Angle 3: \\( 69 \\times 3600 + 36 \\times 60 + 20 = 250580 \\) seconds\n- Angle 4: \\( 22 \\times 3600 + 17 \\times 60 + 02 = 80222 \\) seconds\n- Angle 5: \\( 30 \\times 3600 + 29 \\times 60 + 25 = 109765 \\) seconds\n- Angle 6: \\( 57 \\times 3600 + 37 \\times 60 + 33 = 207453 \\) seconds\n- Angle 7: \\( 50 \\times 3600 + 35 \\times 60 + 44 = 182744 \\) seconds\n- Angle 8: \\( 41 \\times 3600 + 17 \\times 60 + 26 = 148646 \\) seconds\n\nTotal sum in seconds:\n\\[ = 105334 + 211280 + 250580 + 80222 + 109765 + 207453 + 182744 + 148646 = 1297024 \\text{ seconds} \\]\n\nConvert this total back to degrees:\n\\[ 1297024 \\div 3600 = 360^\\circ + 22^\\circ \\]\n\\[ 1297024 \\mod 3600 = 3224 \\text{ seconds} \\]\n\nConvert remaining seconds:\n\\[ 3224 \\div 60 = 53' \\]\n\\[ 3224 \\mod 60 = 44'' \\]\n\nThus, the total is 360\u00b022'53'' which indicates spherical excess adjustment.\n\nAdjust Option A to match closest to observed values:\nA. \n\\[ \\text{1} = \\text{28}^\\circ \\text{25}'\\text{32.66}'' \\]\netc.\n\nCheck the logic. The closest match given is the expected first angle adjustment:\n\\[ 29\\text{\u00b0}25'34'' \\rightarrow 28\\text{\u00b0