"To determine the stations for the Point of Curvature (P.C.) and Point of Tangency (P.T.), we need to use the given information:\n\n1. **Intersection angle (I)**: \\(16^\\circ41'\\)\n2. **Degree of curvature (D)**: \\(5^\\circ40'\\)\n3. **P.I.** = \\(56 + 77.21\\)\n\n### Steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the Radius (R):**\n   \\[\n   R = \\frac{5729.58}{D} = \\frac{5729.58}{5.6667} \\approx 1011.24 \\text{ ft}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the Length of the Curve (L):**\n   \\[\n   L = \\frac{I \\times \\pi \\times R}{180} \n   \\]\n   - First, convert \\(I\\) to decimal: \\(I = 16 + \\frac{41}{60} = 16.6833\\) degrees.\n   \\[\n   L = \\frac{16.6833 \\times \\pi \\times 1011.24}{180} \\approx 294.41 \\text{ ft}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the Tangent Distance (T):**\n   \\[\n   T = R \\times \\tan\\left(\\frac{I}{2}\\right)\n   \\]\n   - Calculate \\(\\frac{I}{2} = 8.3417^\\circ\\) and \\(\\tan(8.3417^\\circ) \\approx 0.14649\\)\n   \\[\n   T = 1011.24 \\times 0.14649 \\approx 148.13 \\text{ ft}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Determine the Stations for P.C. and P.T.:**\n\n   - **Calculate P.C.:** Subtract \\(T\\) from P.I.:\n     \\[\n     \\text{P.C.} = 56 + 77.21 - 1.4813 \\approx 55 + 38.96\n     \\]\n\n   - **Calculate P.T.:** Add \\(L\\) to P.C.:\n     \\[\n     \\text{P.T.} = 55 + 38.96 + 2.9441 \\approx 58 + 23.37\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:\n\nANSWER: A"
