"To calculate the distance of S from C, let's first understand the measurements provided and how they relate to triangles.\n\n1. **Calculate Angles at S**:\n   - The angle \\( \\angle ASB \\) is calculated using the readings: \n     \\[\n     \\angle ASB = 74\u00b030'35\" - 14\u00b043'27\" = 59\u00b047'08\"\n     \\]\n\n   - The angle \\( \\angle BSC \\) is:\n     \\[\n     \\angle BSC = 227\u00b018'12\" - 74\u00b030'35\" = 152\u00b047'37\"\n     \\]\n\n   - The angle \\( \\angle ASC \\) can then be found using angle sum in a triangle:\n     \\[\n     \\angle ASC = 360\u00b0 - (59\u00b047'08\" + 152\u00b047'37\") = 147\u00b025'15\"\n     \\]\n\n2. **Use Sine Rule in Triangle ASC**:\n   - Given lengths are \\( AC = 17495 \\, m \\) and \\( BC = 13672 \\, m \\). Angle \\( \\angle ACB = 59\u00b044'53\" \\).\n   - Using the Sine Rule to find CS:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{CS}{\\sin(\\angle ASC)} = \\frac{AC}{\\sin(\\angle ACB)}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Calculate CS**:\n   - First, calculate \\( \\sin \\) values:\n     - \\( \\sin(\\angle ACB) \\): Convert \\( 59\u00b044'53\" \\) to decimal: \\( 59.7481\u00b0 \\).\n     - \\( \\sin(59.7481\u00b0) \\approx 0.863 \\)\n\n     - \\( \\sin(\\angle ASC) \\): Convert \\( 147\u00b025'15\" \\) to decimal: \\( 147.4208\u00b0 \\).\n     - \\( \\sin(147.4208\u00b0) \\approx 0.545 \\)\n\n   - Using Sine Rule:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{CS}{0.545} = \\frac{17495}{0.863}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     CS = \\frac{17495 \\times 0.545}{0.863}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     CS \\approx 10.792 \\, m\n     \\]\n\nThus, the distance of S from C is approximately 10.792 m.\n\nANSWER: C"
