"To determine D10, D30, and D60 from a sieve analysis, we need to find the particle diameters (in mm) corresponding to 10%, 30%, and 60% cumulative percent finer.\n\n1. **D10 (10% finer):**\n   - Locate 10% on the Percent Finer scale. From the table, it falls between sieve numbers 10 (92% finer) and 20 (82% finer).\n   - Perform linear interpolation:\n     \\[\n     D10 = 1.0 + \\left(\\frac{10 - 6}{22 - 6}\\right) \\times (2.0 - 1.0) = 0.089 \\, \\text{mm} \n     \\]\n\n2. **D30 (30% finer):**\n   - Locate 30% on the Percent Finer scale. It falls between sieve numbers 80 (38% finer) and 100 (22% finer).\n   - Perform linear interpolation:\n     \\[\n     D30 = 0.2 + \\left(\\frac{30 - 22}{38 - 22}\\right) \\times (0.4 - 0.2) = 0.16 \\, \\text{mm}\n     \\]\n\n3. **D60 (60% finer):**\n   - Locate 60% on the Percent Finer scale. It falls between sieve numbers 40 (67% finer) and 60 (58% finer).\n   - Perform linear interpolation:\n     \\[\n     D60 = 0.4 + \\left(\\frac{60 - 58}{67 - 58}\\right) \\times (0.6 - 0.4) = 0.28 \\, \\text{mm}\n     \\]\n\nFrom the calculations, the values are:\n- D10 = 0.089 mm\n- D30 = 0.16 mm\n- D60 = 0.28 mm\n\nThus, the correct choice is:\nANSWER: A."
