"To determine the name of Light #3 in the three-point lighting setup, we need to understand the roles of each light in the setup:\n\n1. **Key Light** - This is the primary light and is usually the strongest. It is placed to one side of the camera/subject to produce some shadows.\n\n2. **Fill Light** - This light is placed opposite the key light. It is used to fill in the shadows created by the key light, usually with a softer light.\n\n3. **Back or Hair Light** - This light is placed behind the subject. It helps separate the subject from the background and highlights contours, especially the subject\u2019s hair and shoulders.\n\nIn the diagram, Light #3 is positioned behind the subject, indicating it is used to separate the subject from the background and add dimension, which aligns with the purpose of the back or hair light.\n\nANSWER: D. Back or Hair Light."
