"To identify which technique is demonstrated in the work on the right, we need to consider what each option represents:\n\nA. Linear perspective: This is a technique used to create the illusion of depth and space on a flat surface, often by drawing lines that converge at a vanishing point in the distance.\n\nB. Hieratic scale: This technique involves the use of size to denote importance, where more important figures are larger in the artwork.\n\nC. Chiaroscuro: This refers to the use of strong contrasts between light and dark to create a sense of volume and three-dimensionality.\n\nD. Inlay: This involves embedding different materials into a surface to create a design.\n\nThe image shows panels on Ghiberti's \"Gates of Paradise,\" known for its use of linear perspective. The panels depict biblical scenes with depth and a three-dimensional illusion, characteristic of linear perspective.\n\nANSWER: A."
