"To determine the type of tissue depicted in the image, we need to analyze the characteristics of the cells:\n\n1. **Simple Cuboidal Epithelium**: This tissue consists of a single layer of cube-shaped cells. The nuclei are spherical and centrally located.\n\n2. **Simple Columnar Epithelium**: This tissue has a single layer of tall and narrow cells. Nuclei are typically elongated and located towards the base.\n\n3. **Transitional Epithelium**: This tissue has multiple layers of cells that can change shape. The cells are rounded when the tissue is not stretched and can appear more squamous when stretched.\n\n4. **Stratified Cuboidal Epithelium**: This tissue consists of multiple layers of cube-shaped cells. However, it typically has only two or three layers.\n\nUpon examining the image:\n- The tissue appears to have multiple layers of cells.\n- The cells at the surface are larger and more rounded, which is characteristic of transitional epithelium.\n\nBased on these observations, the tissue in the image is most consistent with transitional epithelium.\n\nANSWER: C"
