"To identify the cellular adaptation shown in the images:\n\n1. **Atrophy**: This is a reduction in cell size and often results in a smaller tissue size. The cells typically appear smaller and less numerous compared to the normal state.\n\n2. **Hypertrophy**: It involves an increase in cell size, leading to larger cells while the number of cells stays the same. This results in an enlarged tissue or organ.\n\n3. **Necrosis**: A form of cell injury which results in the premature death of cells in living tissue. It often appears with cell swelling, rupture, and fragmentation.\n\n4. **Aplasia**: This is a defect where an organ or tissue is absent or underdeveloped due to the failure of cells to proliferate.\n\n**Image Analysis**:\n- The normal cells on the left side appear densely packed and of normal size.\n- The cells on the right side are larger and show increased cell size compared to the left.\n\n**Conclusion**: The right-side image shows an increase in cell size indicating hypertrophy.\n\nANSWER: B. Hypertrophy."
