"To determine the type of tissue in the image, let's analyze the characteristics:\n\n1. **Simple Cuboidal Epithelium**: These cells are cube-shaped and have a similar height and width. They are usually a single layer.\n\n2. **Simple Columnar Epithelium**: These cells are tall and column-like, forming a single layer.\n\n3. **Simple Squamous Epithelium**: These cells are flat and thin, forming a single layer that looks like a tile floor.\n\n4. **Pseudostratified Epithelium**: Although these cells appear to have multiple layers, all cells are in contact with the basement membrane. The nuclei appear at various heights.\n\nFrom the image:\n\n- The cells appear to have nuclei at different levels, which aligns with the description of pseudostratified epithelium.\n- It does not look like the single-layer organization seen in simple squamous, cuboidal, or columnar epithelia.\n\nANSWER: D"
