"To determine the sequence of the newly synthesized leading strand, we need to examine the DNA replication process:\n\n1. **Understanding DNA Replication**: DNA replication involves synthesizing a new strand using the template strand. Replication proceeds in the 5' to 3' direction.\n\n2. **Identifying the Template for the Leading Strand**: \n   - The leading strand is synthesized continuously in the direction of the replication fork. \n   - In the provided sequence for Region 1:\n     - Top strand: 5'-TAAACCG-3'\n     - Bottom strand: 3'-ATTTGGC-5'\n\n3. **Directionality and Synthesis**:\n   - The replication fork moves from left to right in Region 1, suggesting the bottom strand serves as the template for continuous synthesis of the leading strand.\n\n4. **Base Pair Complementarity**:\n   - The newly synthesized leading strand will be complementary to the bottom template strand:\n     - Bottom strand (template): 3'-ATTTGGC-5'\n     - Complementary sequence (new strand in 5' to 3' direction): 5'-TAACCG-3'\n\nThus, the newly synthesized leading strand in Region 1 is: 5'-TAACCG-3'.\n\nGiven the options:\nA. 5'-CGGTTTA-3'\nB. 5'-TAAACCG-3'\nC. 5'-GCCAAAT-3'\nD. 5'-ATTTGGC-3'\n\nThe correct choice is:\nANSWER: B"
