"To determine the mRNA sequence transcribed from the given template strand, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the Template Strand:** \n   The provided sequence is the template strand, running from 3' to 5'.\n\n2. **Find the Promoter Region (TATA Box):**\n   The TATA box is commonly found in the sequence as TATAAT. In this sequence, it appears at the beginning. \n\n3. **Determine the Transcription Start Site:**\n   Transcription typically starts a few bases downstream of the TATA box. If we assume it starts immediately after the TATA box, locate the start at the beginning of the sequence.\n\n4. **Transcribe the mRNA:**\n   The mRNA is synthesized complementary to the DNA template (3' to 5'), and it runs from 5' to 3'. DNA adenine (A) pairs with mRNA uracil (U), thymine (T) with adenine (A), cytosine (C) with guanine (G), and guanine (G) with cytosine (C).\n   \n   DNA Template: 3' - TACCTATAATCTCAATTGATAGAAGGCACTCTTAC - 5'\n   mRNA Sequence: 5' - AUGGAUAUUAGAGUUAACUAUCUUCCGUGAGAUG - 3'\n\n   Initiation typically involves recognizing the start codon (AUG) which is already two bases into the mRNA (starting from the 5' of the TATA box sequence).\n\n5. **Select the Correct Option:**\n   Based on the transcribed sequence, choose the corresponding letter choice.\n\nANSWER: D"
