"To determine which statement is false, we need to understand the correct hierarchical relationships in biology.\n\nA. Tissues exist within organs which exist within organ systems.\n   - This is a true statement. Tissues combine to form organs, and organs work together to form organ systems.\n\nB. Communities exist within populations which exist within ecosystems.\n   - This is a false statement. Populations consist of individuals of the same species, communities are made up of different populations, and ecosystems include communities and their physical environments.\n\nC. Organelles exist within cells which exist within tissues.\n   - This is a true statement. Organelles are components of cells, which form tissues.\n\nD. Communities exist within ecosystems which exist in the biosphere.\n   - This is a true statement. Communities are part of ecosystems, and ecosystems are part of the biosphere.\n\nTherefore, the false statement is:\n\nANSWER: B."
