"To predict the sign of the change in enthalpy, \\(\\Delta H\\), we can use Le Chatelier's principle. According to Le Chatelier\u2019s principle:\n\n- If an endothermic reaction (absorbs heat) is affected by an increase in temperature, the reaction shifts to the right, favoring the formation of products.\n- If an exothermic reaction (releases heat) is affected by an increase in temperature, the reaction shifts to the left, favoring the formation of reactants.\n\nObserving the data:\n\n- At \\(700^\\circ\\text{C}\\), the percentage of \\(CO\\) is \\(60\\%\\).\n- At \\(850^\\circ\\text{C}\\), the percentage of \\(CO\\) increases to \\(94\\%\\).\n\nAs the temperature increases, the concentration of \\(CO\\) increases, indicating the reaction shifts to the right. This suggests that the forward reaction is endothermic, as it is favored by an increase in temperature.\n\nTherefore, the sign of \\(\\Delta H\\) is positive.\n\nANSWER: A."
