"To find the average waiting time, we need to calculate the waiting time for each process, then average them. The waiting time for a process is the total time the process has been in the ready queue.\n\n1. **Process P1**: \n   - Starts at time 0, so waiting time is 0.\n\n2. **Process P2**: \n   - Starts execution at time 10.\n   - Waiting time = 10 - 0 = 10.\n\n3. **Process P3**: \n   - Starts execution at time 39.\n   - Waiting time = 39 - 0 = 39.\n\n4. **Process P4**: \n   - Starts execution at time 42.\n   - Waiting time = 42 - 0 = 42.\n\n5. **Process P5**: \n   - Starts execution at time 49.\n   - Waiting time = 49 - 0 = 49.\n\nNow, compute the average waiting time:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Average waiting time} = \\frac{0 + 10 + 39 + 42 + 49}{5} = \\frac{140}{5} = 28\n\\]\n\nANSWER: C"
