"To solve this problem, let's calculate each of the metrics using the confusion matrix provided.\n\n1. **Accuracy**: The ratio of correctly predicted instances to the total instances.  \n   \\[\n   \\text{Accuracy} = \\frac{\\text{True Positives} + \\text{True Negatives}}{\\text{Total}} = \\frac{100 + 50}{165} = \\frac{150}{165} \\approx 0.91\n   \\]\n\n2. **Misclassification Rate**: The ratio of incorrectly predicted instances to the total instances.  \n   \\[\n   \\text{Misclassification Rate} = \\frac{\\text{False Positives} + \\text{False Negatives}}{\\text{Total}} = \\frac{10 + 5}{165} = \\frac{15}{165} \\approx 0.09\n   \\]\n\n3. **True Negative Rate (Specificity)**: The ratio of correctly predicted negative instances to the total actual negative instances.  \n   \\[\n   \\text{True Negative Rate} = \\frac{\\text{True Negatives}}{\\text{True Negatives} + \\text{False Positives}} = \\frac{50}{50 + 10} = \\frac{50}{60} \\approx 0.83\n   \\]\n\n4. **True Positive Rate (Sensitivity or Recall)**: The ratio of correctly predicted positive instances to the total actual positive instances.  \n   \\[\n   \\text{True Positive Rate} = \\frac{\\text{True Positives}}{\\text{True Positives} + \\text{False Negatives}} = \\frac{100}{100 + 5} = \\frac{100}{105} \\approx 0.95\n   \\]\n\nNow, let's check the given options with these calculations:\n\n1. Accuracy is ~0.91: True.\n2. Misclassification rate is ~0.91: False.\n3. True Negative rate is ~0.95: False.\n4. True positive rate is ~0.95: True.\n\nMatching with options:\n\nA. 1 and 3. (False)\nB. 2 and 4. (False)\nC. 1 and 4. (True)\nD. 2 and 3. (False)\n\nANSWER: C."
