"To determine if the schedule is serial or nonserial, we need to check the order of operations between transactions \\( T_1 \\) and \\( T_2 \\).\n\n1. **Serial Schedule:** All actions of one transaction are completed before any action of the other transaction starts.\n2. **Nonserial Schedule:** Actions of one transaction interleave with actions of the other.\n\nLet's analyze the schedule:\n\n- \\( T_1 \\) starts with `read_item(X); X := X - N; write_item(X)`.\n- Then \\( T_2 \\) performs `read_item(X); X := X + M; write_item(X)`.\n- After \\( T_2 \\) completes, \\( T_1 \\) resumes with `read_item(Y); Y := Y + N; write_item(Y)`.\n\nSince actions of \\( T_1 \\) are interleaved with actions of \\( T_2 \\), the schedule is nonserial.\n\nANSWER: B. nonserial."
