"To calculate the TLB miss latency:\n\n1. **Guest OS Page Table Walk:**\n   - 3 levels of page tables need to be accessed.\n   - Each level table access takes 50 cycles.\n   - Total cycles for guest page walk = 3 levels \u00d7 50 cycles = 150 cycles.\n\n2. **VMM (Virtual Machine Monitor) Shadow Page Table Walk:**\n   - The host also has 3 levels of page tables.\n   - For each guest level page table access, a corresponding shadow page table access is required.\n   - Total cycles for VMM shadow page walk = 3 levels \u00d7 50 cycles = 150 cycles.\n   \n3. **Total Latency:**\n   - Memory latency for guest + shadow = 150 cycles + 150 cycles = 300 cycles.\n   - Plus 1 cycle TLB access.\n   - Total TLB miss latency = 300 cycles + 1 cycle = 301 cycles.\n\nANSWER: C."
