"To calculate the average wait time, we need to determine the waiting time for each process.\n\n1. **Process P1**:\n   - P1 runs multiple times in the Gantt chart.\n   - First run: Starts at 0, finishes at 4. Wait time before first run = 0.\n   - Second run: Starts at 10, having waited 6 additional units (10 - 4).\n   - Third run: Starts at 14, having waited 0 additional units (continues from 10).\n   - Fourth run: Starts at 18, having waited 0 additional units (continues from 14).\n   - Fifth run: Starts at 22, having waited 0 additional units (continues from 18).\n   - Sixth run: Starts at 26, having waited 0 additional units (continues from 22).\n   - Total wait time for P1 = 0 + 6 + 0 + 0 + 0 + 0 = 6 milliseconds.\n\n2. **Process P2**:\n   - Starts at 4, finishes at 7. Wait time before starting = 4 milliseconds.\n\n3. **Process P3**:\n   - Starts at 7, finishes at 10. Wait time before starting = 7 milliseconds.\n\n**Average Waiting Time Calculation**:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Average Waiting Time} = \\frac{\\text{Total Wait Time}}{\\text{Number of Processes}} = \\frac{6 + 4 + 7}{3} = \\frac{17}{3} = 5.67 \\text{ milliseconds (rounded to two decimal places)}\n\\]\n\nANSWER: A"
