"To find the total end-to-end delay for sending a packet through all three links, we need to consider both the transmission delay and the propagation delay for each link.\n\n### Transmission Delay\nThe transmission delay is calculated as:\n\n\\[ \\text{Transmission Delay} = \\frac{\\text{Packet Length (bits)}}{\\text{Transmission Rate (bps)}} \\]\n\n**Link 1:**\n\n- Packet length = 8000 bits\n- Transmission rate = 100 Mbps = \\(100 \\times 10^6\\) bps\n\n\\[ \\text{Transmission Delay (Link 1)} = \\frac{8000}{100 \\times 10^6} = 8.00 \\times 10^{-5} \\text{ seconds} \\]\n\n**Link 2:**\n\n- Transmission rate = 100 Mbps = \\(100 \\times 10^6\\) bps\n\n\\[ \\text{Transmission Delay (Link 2)} = \\frac{8000}{100 \\times 10^6} = 8.00 \\times 10^{-5} \\text{ seconds} \\]\n\n**Link 3:**\n\n- Transmission rate = 10 Mbps = \\(10 \\times 10^6\\) bps\n\n\\[ \\text{Transmission Delay (Link 3)} = \\frac{8000}{10 \\times 10^6} = 8.00 \\times 10^{-4} \\text{ seconds} \\]\n\n### Propagation Delay\nThe propagation delay is calculated as:\n\n\\[ \\text{Propagation Delay} = \\frac{\\text{Link Length (m)}}{\\text{Speed of Light (m/s)}} \\]\n\n- Speed of light = \\(3 \\times 10^8\\) m/s\n\n**Link 1:**\n\n- Link length = 1 km = 1000 m\n\n\\[ \\text{Propagation Delay (Link 1)} = \\frac{1000}{3 \\times 10^8} = 3.33 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{ seconds} \\]\n\n**Link 2:**\n\n- Link length = 500 km = 500,000 m\n\n\\[ \\text{Propagation Delay (Link 2)} = \\frac{500,000}{3 \\times 10^8} = 1.67 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{ seconds} \\]\n\n**Link 3:**\n\n- Link length = 3 km = 3000 m\n\n\\[ \\text{Propagation Delay (Link 3)} = \\frac{3000}{3 \\times 10^8} = 1.00 \\times 10^{-5} \\text{ seconds} \\]\n\n### Total Delay for Each Link\n\n**Total Delay (Link 1):**  \n\\[ 8.00 \\times 10^{-5} + 3.33 \\times 10^{-6} = 8.33 \\times 10^{-5} \\text{ seconds} \\]\n\n**Total Delay (Link 2):**  \n\\[ 8.00 \\times 10^{-5} + 1.67 \\times 10^{-3} = 1.75 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{ seconds} \\]\n\n**Total Delay (Link 3):**  \n\\[ 8.00 \\times 10^{-4} + 1.00 \\times 10^{-5} = 8.10 \\times 10^{-4} \\text{ seconds} \\]\n\n### Total End-to-End Delay\nSum of delays for all links:\n\n\\[ 8.33 \\times 10^{-5} + 1.75 \\times 10^{-3} + 8.10 \\times 10^{-4} = 2.61 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{ seconds} \\]\n\nTherefore, the total end-to-end delay is:\n\nANSWER: 2.61e-3"
