"To find the average wait time, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Determine the Burst Time for Each Process:**\n   - From the Gantt chart, P1 runs from time 0 to 24, so burst time = 24ms.\n   - P2 runs from time 24 to 27, so burst time = 3ms.\n   - P3 runs from time 27 to 30, so burst time = 3ms.\n\n2. **Calculate the Completion Time for Each Process:**\n   - Completion time for P1 = 24ms\n   - Completion time for P2 = 27ms\n   - Completion time for P3 = 30ms\n\n3. **Calculate the Waiting Time for Each Process:**\n   - Waiting time is calculated as: \\( \\text{Waiting Time} = \\text{Turnaround Time} - \\text{Burst Time} \\)\n   - Turnaround time = Completion time (since all processes arrived at time 0)\n\n   - Waiting time for P1 = 24ms (turnaround) - 24ms (burst) = 0ms\n   - Waiting time for P2 = 27ms (turnaround) - 3ms (burst) = 24ms\n   - Waiting time for P3 = 30ms (turnaround) - 3ms (burst) = 27ms\n\n4. **Calculate the Average Waiting Time:**\n   - Average waiting time = (0 + 24 + 27) / 3 = 51 / 3 = 17ms\n\nANSWER: B"
