"To calculate recall, use the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{Recall} = \\frac{\\text{True Positives}}{\\text{True Positives} + \\text{False Negatives}} \\]\n\nIn this context:\n- True Positives (Relevant and Retrieved) = 2000\n- False Negatives (Relevant but Not Retrieved) = 4000\n\nNow, plug in the values:\n\n\\[ \\text{Recall} = \\frac{2000}{2000 + 4000} = \\frac{2000}{6000} = \\frac{1}{3} \\approx 0.33 \\]\n\nConvert this into a percentage:\n\n\\[ 0.33 \\times 100\\% = 33\\% \\]\n\nANSWER: A."
