teration:**  \n   - Choose the vertex with the smallest tentative distance, which is \\( G \\) (Distance 8).\n   - Update the distance for \\( T \\) from \\( G \\): Distance \\( 11 \\) through \\( S \\to A \\to C \\to E \\to G \\to T \\).\n\n9. **Eighth Iteration:**  \n   - Choose the vertex with the smallest tentative distance, which is \\( T \\) (Distance 9).\n\nGiven Dijkstra's algorithm explores nodes in order of their shortest known distance, the path \\( S \\to A \\to C \\to E \\to T \\) (option C) is chosen as it was the first shortest path to be found with a total weight of 9.\n\nANSWER: C"
