"In a recursive DNS query:\n\n1. The requesting host sends a query to the local DNS server.\n2. The local DNS server performs a recursive query to the Root DNS server.\n3. The Root DNS server responds with the address of a TLD DNS server.\n4. The local DNS server queries the TLD DNS server.\n5. The TLD DNS server responds with the address of the authoritative DNS server.\n6. The local DNS server queries the authoritative DNS server.\n7. The authoritative DNS server returns the requested IP address back to the **local DNS server**.\n8. The local DNS server forwards the final result to the requesting host.\n\nBetween steps 4 and 5 in a recursive query, the authoritative DNS server forwards the response to the local DNS server.\n\nANSWER: B. DNS Local."
