"To determine the maximum number of users that can be supported with circuit switching, we need to calculate based on the bandwidth each user requires.\n\nEach user requires 10 Mbps of bandwidth, and the total available bandwidth is 150 Mbps.\n\nMaximum number of circuit-switched users (\\(N_{cs}\\)) can be calculated as follows:\n\n\\[\nN_{cs} = \\frac{\\text{Total Available Bandwidth}}{\\text{Bandwidth per User}} = \\frac{150 \\text{ Mbps}}{10 \\text{ Mbps}} = 15\n\\]\n\nSo, the maximum number of users that can be supported using circuit switching is 15.\n\nANSWER: A"
