"To calculate the average wait time, we first need to determine the wait time for each process. The wait time is the total time a process spends waiting in the ready queue before it gets the CPU for execution. \n\nFrom the Gantt chart:\n\n- **P2** starts execution at time 0, so its wait time is 0 milliseconds.\n- **P3** starts execution at time 3 (after P2 finishes), so its wait time is 3 milliseconds.\n- **P1** starts execution at time 6 (after P3 finishes), so its wait time is 6 milliseconds.\n\nNow calculate the average wait time:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Average Wait Time} = \\frac{\\text{Wait Time of P2} + \\text{Wait Time of P3} + \\text{Wait Time of P1}}{3} = \\frac{0 + 3 + 6}{3} = \\frac{9}{3} = 3 \\text{ milliseconds}\n\\]\n\nAnswer choices (in alphabetical order):\n\nA. 3 milliseconds\n\nANSWER: A"
