"To calculate the standard deviation of returns for both stocks, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the Expected Return for each Stock:**\n\n   - **Stock X:**\n     \\[\n     E(X) = (0.2 \\times -20\\%) + (0.5 \\times 18\\%) + (0.3 \\times 50\\%) = -4\\% + 9\\% + 15\\% = 20\\%\n     \\]\n\n   - **Stock Y:**\n     \\[\n     E(Y) = (0.2 \\times -15\\%) + (0.5 \\times 20\\%) + (0.3 \\times 10\\%) = -3\\% + 10\\% + 3\\% = 10\\%\n     \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the Variance for each Stock:**\n   \n   - **Stock X Variance:**\n     \\[\n     \\begin{align*}\n     \\sigma^2(X) &= (0.2 \\times (-20\\% - 20\\%)^2) + (0.5 \\times (18\\% - 20\\%)^2) + (0.3 \\times (50\\% - 20\\%)^2) \\\\\n     &= 0.2 \\times 1600 + 0.5 \\times 4 + 0.3 \\times 900 \\\\\n     &= 320 + 2 + 270 \\\\\n     &= 592\n     \\end{align*}\n     \\]\n\n   - **Stock Y Variance:**\n     \\[\n     \\begin{align*}\n     \\sigma^2(Y) &= (0.2 \\times (-15\\% - 10\\%)^2) + (0.5 \\times (20\\% - 10\\%)^2) + (0.3 \\times (10\\% - 10\\%)^2) \\\\\n     &= 0.2 \\times 625 + 0.5 \\times 100 + 0.3 \\times 0 \\\\\n     &= 125 + 50 + 0 \\\\\n     &= 175\n     \\end{align*}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the Standard Deviation for each Stock:**\n\n   - **Stock X:**\n     \\[\n     \\sigma(X) = \\sqrt{592} \\approx 24.33\\%\n     \\]\n\n   - **Stock Y:**\n     \\[\n     \\sigma(Y) = \\sqrt{175} \\approx 13.23\\%\n     \\]\n\nANSWER: B. 24.33%, 13.23%."
