"To calculate the company cost of capital, we use the Weighted Average Cost of Capital (WACC) formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{WACC} = \\left( \\frac{E}{V} \\cdot r_{\\text{equity}} \\right) + \\left( \\frac{D}{V} \\cdot r_{\\text{debt}} \\right) \\]\n\nWhere:\n- \\( E \\) is the market value of equity.\n- \\( D \\) is the market value of debt.\n- \\( V \\) is the total market value of the company's financing (equity + debt).\n- \\( r_{\\text{equity}} \\) is the expected return on equity (15% or 0.15).\n- \\( r_{\\text{debt}} \\) is the yield to maturity on debt (8% or 0.08).\n\n1. **Calculate \\( E \\) (Market Value of Equity):**\n\n   Number of shares = 10,000\n\n   Price per share = $50\n\n   \\[ E = 10,000 \\times 50 = 500,000 \\]\n\n2. **Calculate \\( D \\) (Market Value of Debt):**\n\n   Given \\( D = 300,000 \\)\n\n3. **Calculate \\( V \\) (Total Market Value):**\n\n   \\[ V = E + D = 500,000 + 300,000 = 800,000 \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the WACC:**\n\n   \\[ \\frac{E}{V} = \\frac{500,000}{800,000} = 0.625 \\]\n\n   \\[ \\frac{D}{V} = \\frac{300,000}{800,000} = 0.375 \\]\n\n   \\[ \\text{WACC} = (0.625 \\times 0.15) + (0.375 \\times 0.08) \\]\n\n   \\[ \\text{WACC} = 0.09375 + 0.03 \\]\n\n   \\[ \\text{WACC} = 0.12375 \\]\n\nTherefore, the company cost of capital is approximately 12.375%, which rounds to 0.128 when using the options provided.\n\nANSWER: C."
