"To find the dry density of the soil layer using the sand pouring method, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the volume of the test pit:**\n\n   \\[\n   V = \\frac{M_s}{\\rho}\n   \\]\n\n   Where:\n   - \\( M_s = 11265.30 \\, \\text{g} \\) (mass of standard sand)\n   - \\( \\rho = 1.62 \\, \\text{g/cm}^3 \\) (density of standard sand)\n\n   \\[\n   V = \\frac{11265.30}{1.62} = 6951.41 \\, \\text{cm}^3\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the dry mass of the soil:**\n\n   \\[\n   m_d = \\frac{m}{1 + \\omega}\n   \\]\n\n   Where:\n   - \\( m = 14320.16 \\, \\text{g} \\) (mass of soil)\n   - \\( \\omega = 0.136 \\) (moisture content)\n\n   \\[\n   m_d = \\frac{14320.16}{1 + 0.136} = 12609.77 \\, \\text{g}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the dry density of the soil:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\rho_d = \\frac{m_d}{V}\n   \\]\n\n   \\[\n   \\rho_d = \\frac{12609.77}{6951.41} = 1.813 \\, \\text{g/cm}^3\n   \\]\n\nBased on the calculations, the closest option for the dry density of the soil layer is:\n\nANSWER: C. 1.81"
