"To solve the problem, we start by analyzing the given wave equation:\n\n\\[ y = -0.02 \\cos \\pi (4x - 50t) \\]\n\nThe general form of a wave equation is:\n\n\\[ y = A \\cos (kx - \\omega t) \\]\n\nwhere:\n- \\( A \\) is the amplitude,\n- \\( k \\) is the wave number,\n- \\( \\omega \\) is the angular frequency.\n\n### Step 1: Identify the Amplitude\n- The amplitude \\( A \\) is the coefficient in front of the cosine, which is \\( -0.02 \\).\n- Since amplitude is a positive quantity, \\( A = 0.02 \\, \\text{m} \\).\n\n### Step 2: Determine the Wavelength\n- The wave number \\( k \\) is related to wavelength \\( \\lambda \\) by the formula: \\( k = \\frac{2\\pi}{\\lambda} \\).\n- From the equation, \\( k = 4\\pi \\).\n- Solve for \\( \\lambda \\):\n  \\[\n  4\\pi = \\frac{2\\pi}{\\lambda} \\implies \\lambda = \\frac{2\\pi}{4\\pi} = \\frac{1}{2} \\, \\text{m} = 0.5 \\, \\text{m}\n  \\]\n\n### Conclusion\nThe amplitude is \\( 0.02 \\, \\text{m} \\) and the wavelength is \\( 0.5 \\, \\text{m} \\).\n\nANSWER: D"
