"To determine the effective value, frequency, and initial phase angle of the excitation signal \\( u(t) = 1.732 \\sin(314t + 30^\\circ) \\) V, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Effective Value (RMS):**  \n   The effective value (RMS) of a sinusoidal voltage \\( V_m \\sin(\\omega t + \\phi) \\) is given by:  \n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{rms}} = \\frac{V_m}{\\sqrt{2}}\n   \\]  \n   Here, \\( V_m = 1.732 \\) V.  \n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{rms}} = \\frac{1.732}{\\sqrt{2}} \\approx 1.225 \\, \\text{V}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Frequency:**  \n   The angular frequency \\( \\omega = 314 \\) rad/s can be converted to frequency \\( f \\) in Hz using the relation:  \n   \\[\n   f = \\frac{\\omega}{2\\pi} = \\frac{314}{2\\pi} \\approx 50 \\, \\text{Hz}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Initial Phase Angle:**  \n   The initial phase angle is given directly in the equation as \\( 30^\\circ \\).\n\nThus, the frequency is 50 Hz, the effective value is approximately 1.225 V, and the initial phase angle is 30\u00b0.\n\nTherefore, the correct choice is: \n\nANSWER: C."
