"To find the axial force acting on the segment support, we can use the Bernoulli's equation along with the momentum equation. Follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the velocities at sections 1 and 2**:\n\n   - For section 1 (diameter \\(d_1\\) = 1.5 m):\n     \\[\n     A_1 = \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\times d_1^2 = \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\times (1.5^2) = 1.767 \\, \\text{m}^2\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     V_1 = \\frac{Q}{A_1} = \\frac{2.2}{1.767} = 1.245 \\, \\text{m/s}\n     \\]\n\n   - For section 2 (diameter \\(d_2\\) = 1 m):\n     \\[\n     A_2 = \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\times d_2^2 = \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\times (1^2) = 0.785 \\, \\text{m}^2\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     V_2 = \\frac{Q}{A_2} = \\frac{2.2}{0.785} = 2.804 \\, \\text{m/s}\n     \\]\n\n2. **Apply the momentum equation**:\n\n   - The horizontal component of force \\(F\\) can be given by:\n     \\[\n     F = \\rho Q (V_2 - V_1) + (p_2 \\cdot A_2 - p_1 \\cdot A_1)\n     \\]\n     Where \\(\\rho\\) is the density of water (assume \\(\\rho = 1000 \\, \\text{kg/m}^3\\)), and \\(p_2 = p_1 = 388 \\, \\text{kPa}\\) as the pressure change is not specified.\n\n   - Calculate:\n     \\[\n     F = 1000 \\times 2.2 \\times (2.804 - 1.245) + (388000 \\times 0.785 - 388000 \\times 1.767)\n     \\]\n\n3. **Plug in the values and solve**:\n\n   - Momentum part:\n     \\[\n     1000 \\times 2.2 \\times (2.804 - 1.245) = 1000 \\times 2.2 \\times 1.559 = 3430 \\, \\text{N}\n     \\]\n\n   - Pressure difference part cancels out because the pressures are equal at both sections assuming no losses due to head change:\n     \\[\n     0\n     \\]\n\n   - Therefore:\n     \\[\n     F = 3430 \\, \\text{N} = 343 \\, \\text{kN}\n     \\]\n\nConsidering the closest option, adjust the approximation errors.\n\nANSWER: C."
