"To determine the ratio of the average flow velocity (\\(v_1/v_2\\)) before and after the sudden expansion, we can use the principle of continuity for incompressible flow. The equation of continuity states:\n\n\\[ A_1 \\cdot v_1 = A_2 \\cdot v_2 \\]\n\nWhere:\n- \\(A_1\\) and \\(A_2\\) are the cross-sectional areas before and after the expansion, respectively.\n- \\(v_1\\) and \\(v_2\\) are the flow velocities before and after the expansion, respectively.\n\nSince the area of a circle is proportional to the square of its diameter, we can express the areas in terms of diameters:\n\\[ A_1 = \\pi \\left(\\frac{d_1}{2}\\right)^2 \\]\n\\[ A_2 = \\pi \\left(\\frac{d_2}{2}\\right)^2 \\]\n\nThe ratio of the areas in terms of the diameters is:\n\\[ \\frac{A_1}{A_2} = \\left(\\frac{d_1}{d_2}\\right)^2 \\]\n\nGiven \\( \\frac{d_1}{d_2} = 0.5 \\), we substitute into the area ratio:\n\\[ \\frac{A_1}{A_2} = (0.5)^2 = 0.25 \\]\n\nUsing the continuity equation:\n\\[ v_1 = \\frac{A_2}{A_1} \\cdot v_2 \\]\n\\[ v_1 = \\frac{1}{0.25} \\cdot v_2 \\]\n\\[ v_1 = 4 \\cdot v_2 \\]\n\nThus, the ratio \\( v_1/v_2 = 4 \\).\n\nANSWER: A"
