"To determine the natural pore ratio (also known as the void ratio, \\( e \\)) of a fully saturated cohesive soil with a natural water content of 60%, we use the following formula:\n\n\\[\ne = w \\times G_s\n\\]\n\nwhere:\n- \\( w \\) is the water content (in decimal form, so 60% becomes 0.6),\n- \\( G_s \\) is the specific gravity of the soil solids (for cohesive soils, this typically ranges from about 2.6 to 2.8; we can assume an average value of 2.7 for calculation).\n\nTherefore:\n\n\\[\ne = 0.6 \\times 2.7 = 1.62\n\\]\n\nMatching this calculated pore ratio with the given options, the closest value is 1.6.\n\nANSWER: C."
