"To calculate the cost-effectiveness ratio (CER) of the project, we need to evaluate the present value of the benefits and the present value of the costs over the project's lifetime.\n\n**Initial Investment:**\n- 1 million yuan (at time 0)\n\n**Annual Benefits:**\n- 200,000 yuan per year for 10 years\n\n**Annual Maintenance Cost:**\n- 8,000 yuan per year for 10 years\n\n**Discount Rate:**\n- 10%\n\n**Present Value (PV) Calculation:**\n\n1. **PV of Benefits:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{PV of Benefits} = 200,000 \\times \\left(\\frac{1 - (1 + 0.10)^{-10}}{0.10}\\right)\n   \\]\n\n2. **PV of Costs:**\n\n   - **Initial Cost:** 1,000,000 yuan\n   - **Maintenance Cost:**\n     \\[\n     \\text{PV of Maintenance} = 8,000 \\times \\left(\\frac{1 - (1 + 0.10)^{-10}}{0.10}\\right)\n     \\]\n\n3. **Net Present Value (NPV) of Costs:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{NPV of Costs} = 1,000,000 + \\text{PV of Maintenance}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Cost-Effectiveness Ratio:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{CER} = \\frac{\\text{PV of Benefits}}{\\text{NPV of Costs}}\n   \\]\n\n**Calculations:**\n\n1. **PV of Benefits:**\n   - \\[\n   \\text{PV of Benefits} = 200,000 \\times \\left(\\frac{1 - (1 + 0.10)^{-10}}{0.10}\\right) \\approx 200,000 \\times 6.1446 \\approx 1,228,920\n   \\]\n\n2. **PV of Maintenance:**\n   - \\[\n   \\text{PV of Maintenance} = 8,000 \\times \\left(\\frac{1 - (1 + 0.10)^{-10}}{0.10}\\right) \\approx 8,000 \\times 6.1446 \\approx 49,157\n   \\]\n\n3. **NPV of Costs:**\n   - \\[\n   \\text{NPV of Costs} = 1,000,000 + 49,157 = 1,049,157\n   \\]\n\n4. **CER:**\n   - \\[\n   \\text{CER} = \\frac{1,228,920}{1,049,157} \\approx 1.171\n   \\]\n\nThe option that matches our calculation is: B. 1.17.\n\nANSWER: B."
