"To determine the dynamic amplification coefficient, we need to understand the relationship between the natural vibration period of the soil layer and the natural vibration period of the structure. The dynamic amplification coefficient is maximized when the natural period of the soil matches that of the structure.\n\nFor cohesive soil, the shear wave velocity \\( V_s \\) can be calculated using the shear modulus \\( G \\) and the mass density \\( \\rho \\):\n\n\\[\nV_s = \\sqrt{\\frac{G}{\\rho}}\n\\]\n\nHowever, without the specific value for \\(\\rho\\), we'll work with the information given:\n\n1. **Natural Period of Soil Layer**: Use the formula for the fundamental period \\( T \\) of a soil layer:\n\n\\[\nT = \\frac{4H}{V_s}\n\\]\n\nWhere \\( H \\) is the thickness of the soil layer.\n\n2. **Calculate \\( V_s \\) with given shear modulus**:\n   Given:\n   - \\( G = 300 \\, \\text{kN/m}^2 = 300,000 \\, \\text{N/m}^2 \\)\n   - Approximate density for cohesive soils like clay: \\( \\rho \\approx 1800 \\, \\text{kg/m}^3 \\) (typical assumption if not given).\n\n\\[\nV_s = \\sqrt{\\frac{300,000}{1800}} \\approx 12.91 \\, \\text{m/s}\n\\]\n\n3. **Determine Natural Period \\( T \\) of Soil Layer**:\n   - \\( H = 12 \\, \\text{m} \\) (thickness of the cohesive soil layer).\n\n\\[\nT = \\frac{4 \\times 12}{12.91} \\approx 3.72 \\, \\text{seconds}\n\\]\n\n4. **Compare with Structure's Natural Period**:\n   - Given natural period of the mudstone layer (for the bridge): \\( 1.2 \\, \\text{seconds} \\)\n\nSince the natural periods don't match, the dynamic amplification coefficient will not be at its maximum. It often reduces the amplification to a standard factor, commonly used value for non-matching periods like this is given as 1.0 to 1.2 based on standard damping and resonant conditions.\n\nGiven the options, the closest standard approximate value is 1.2.\n\nANSWER: B."
