"To calculate the effective internal friction angle (\\(\\phi'\\)) of the sand, we can use the following steps:\n\n1. **Determine the effective stresses:**\n\n   - Confining pressure (\\(\\sigma_3\\)) = 150 kPa\n   - Vertical pressure at failure (\\(\\sigma_1\\)) = 350 kPa (since 3 times 50 kPa = 150 kPa + 200 kPa = 350 kPa)\n   - Measured pore water pressure (u) = 50 kPa\n\n   The effective stresses are calculated by subtracting the pore water pressure from the total stresses:\n\n   - Effective minor principal stress (\\(\\sigma'_3\\)) = \\(\\sigma_3 - u = 150 - 50 = 100\\) kPa\n   - Effective major principal stress (\\(\\sigma'_1\\)) = \\(\\sigma_1 - u = 350 - 50 = 300\\) kPa\n\n2. **Calculate the effective internal friction angle (\\(\\phi'\\)):**\n\n   Use the triaxial test relationship:\n\n   \\[\n   \\tan(\\phi') = \\frac{\\sigma'_1 - \\sigma'_3}{\\sigma'_1 + \\sigma'_3}\n   \\]\n\n   \\[\n   \\tan(\\phi') = \\frac{300 - 100}{300 + 100} = \\frac{200}{400} = 0.5\n   \\]\n\n   \\[\n   \\phi' = \\tan^{-1}(0.5)\n   \\]\n\n   \\[\n   \\phi' \\approx 26.6\u00b0\n   \\]\n\nThus, the closest option is **A. 23.6\u00b0**.\n\nANSWER: A"
"To determine the load capacity of the composite foundation, we can use the following formula:\n\n\\[ q_s = F_{sk} \\times (1 - n \\times \\eta) + F_{pk} \\times n \\times \\eta \\]\n\nWhere:\n- \\( F_{sk} \\) is the bearing capacity of the soft soil, which is 60 kPa.\n- \\( n \\) is the pile-soil stress ratio, which is 8.5.\n- \\( \\eta \\) is the displacement rate of the mixing pile area, which is 20% or 0.2.\n- \\( F_{pk} \\) is the bearing capacity of the pile, calculated as \\( F_{pk} = n \\times F_{sk} \\).\n\nFirst, calculate \\( F_{pk} \\):\n\n\\[ F_{pk} = n \\times F_{sk} = 8.5 \\times 60 = 510 \\text{ kPa} \\]\n\nNow, plug the values into the formula:\n\n\\[ q_s = 60 \\times (1 - 8.5 \\times 0.2) + 510 \\times 8.5 \\times 0.2 \\]\n\nSimplify the equation:\n\n- First term: \\( 60 \\times (1 - 1.7) = 60 \\times (-0.7) = -42 \\)\n- Second term: \\( 510 \\times 8.5 \\times 0.2 = 867 \\)\n\nNow combine the terms:\n\n\\[ q_s = -42 + 867 = 825 \\text{ kPa} \\]\n\nSince we must select the closest load capacity from the given options, it seems there is an error because the calculated value doesn't directly match any options. Double check whether there may have been a misunderstanding or misrepresentation of the formula.\n\nGiven options:\nA. 120 kPa\nB. 150 kPa\nC. 180 kPa\nD. 200 kPa\n\nAssuming a closer estimate fitting the options:\n\n\\[ q_s = F_{sk} \\times (1-\\eta) + F_{pk} \\times \\eta \\]\n\\[ q_s = 60 \\times 0.8 + 510 \\times 0.2 = 48 + 102 \\]\n\nNow, correctly simplifying:\n\\[ q_s = 150 \\text{ kPa} \\]\n\nANSWER: B"
