"To determine the maximum axial force in the rod, we need to evaluate the forces acting on each section.\n\n1. **Left Section**:\n   - A force of 3 kN is acting to the left.\n\n2. **Middle Section**:\n   - A force of 8 kN is acting to the right.\n\n3. **Right Section**:\n   - A force of 5 kN is acting to the right.\n\nThe resultant forces in each section can be calculated by considering the balance of forces:\n\n- **Resultant Force Calculation**: \n  - Net force in the left section will be \\(8 \\text{ kN (to the right)} - 3 \\text{ kN (to the left)} = 5 \\text{ kN (to the right)}\\).\n  - The middle section is directly subjected to the 8 kN force.\n  - The right section has a net force calculation of \\(5 \\text{ kN (to the right)} + 8 \\text{ kN (to the left in the middle section)} = 3 \\text{ kN (net effect)}\\).\n\nThus, the maximum axial force in the rod is 8 kN, which is the highest force present among the calculated section forces.\n\nANSWER: A."
"To determine the final settlement of the overconsolidated clay layer, we can use the formula for settlement \\( S \\) for a clay layer undergoing recompression:\n\n\\[ \nS = \\frac{H \\cdot (Cc / (1 + e0)) \\cdot \\log_{10}((P0 + Pc) / Pc)} \\]\n\nwhere:  \n- \\( H = 4.0 \\, \\text{m} \\) (thickness of the clay layer),\n- \\( Cc = 0.3 \\) (compression index),\n- \\( e0 = 0.8 \\) (initial porosity ratio),\n- \\( Pc = 400 \\, \\text{kPa} \\) (preconsolidation pressure),\n- \\( P0 = 300 \\, \\text{kPa} \\) (average additional stress).\n\nSince \\( P0 + Pc = 300 + 400 = 700 \\, \\text{kPa} \\), substitute the values into the formula:\n\n\\[ \nS = \\frac{4.0 \\cdot (0.3 / (1 + 0.8)) \\cdot \\log_{10}(700 / 400)} \n\\]\n\nCalculate each component:\n\n1. \\( 1 + e0 = 1.8 \\)\n2. \\( \\frac{Cc}{1 + e0} = \\frac{0.3}{1.8} = 0.1667 \\)\n3. \\( \\log_{10}(700 / 400) = \\log_{10}(1.75) \\approx 0.243 \\)\n\nNow substitute back:\n\n\\[ \nS = 4.0 \\cdot 0.1667 \\cdot 0.243 \\approx 0.162 \\, \\text{m} = 16.2 \\, \\text{cm}\n\\]\n\nConsidering the precision and conversion, the closest option is:\n\nANSWER: C."
