"To find the equivalent horizontal seepage coefficient (\\(k_{eq}\\)) for the layered soil above the impermeable bedrock, we use the formula:\n\n\\[\nk_{eq} = \\frac{\\sum (k_i \\cdot h_i)}{\\sum h_i}\n\\]\n\nWhere:\n- \\(k_i\\) is the permeability coefficient of each layer.\n- \\(h_i\\) is the thickness of each layer.\n\nGiven:\n- Layer 1: \\(k_1 = 1 \\, \\text{m/d}\\), \\(h_1 = 4 \\, \\text{m}\\)\n- Layer 2: \\(k_2 = 2 \\, \\text{m/d}\\), \\(h_2 = 2 \\, \\text{m}\\)\n- Layer 3: \\(k_3 = 4 \\, \\text{m/d}\\), \\(h_3 = 1 \\, \\text{m}\\)\n\nCalculate:\n\n\\[\nk_{eq} = \\frac{(1 \\cdot 4) + (2 \\cdot 2) + (4 \\cdot 1)}{4 + 2 + 1}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nk_{eq} = \\frac{4 + 4 + 4}{7}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nk_{eq} = \\frac{12}{7} = 1.714 \\, \\text{m/d}\n\\]\n\nANSWER: 1.714"
