"To find the angular momentum of the rod, we can use the formula for the angular momentum \\( L \\) of a rotating object:\n\n\\[ L = I \\omega \\]\n\nwhere:\n- \\( I \\) is the moment of inertia,\n- \\( \\omega \\) is the angular velocity.\n\nFor a rod rotating about an axis at one end, the moment of inertia \\( I \\) is:\n\n\\[ I = \\frac{1}{3}ml^2 \\]\n\nSubstitute \\( I \\) into the angular momentum formula:\n\n\\[ L = \\left(\\frac{1}{3}ml^2\\right) \\omega \\]\n\nFrom the given options, to match the format, we simplify it if it appears as:\n\n\\[ L = \\frac{1}{3}ml(\\omega l) \\]\n\nThis matches with option D.\n\nANSWER: D"
