"To solve this, let's analyze each option with the given waveform characteristics:\n\n1. **Option A: The effective value is 10V.**\n   - The effective (RMS) value for a sinusoidal wave with a peak value \\( V_m \\) is \\( V_m / \\sqrt{2} \\). \n   - Here, the peak value \\( V_m \\) is 10V.\n   - Thus, the RMS value is \\( 10V / \\sqrt{2} \\approx 7.07V \\).\n   - This option is incorrect.\n\n2. **Option B: Angular frequency is 314 rad/s.**\n   - Angular frequency \\( \\omega \\) is related to the period \\( T \\) by \\( \\omega = 2\\pi/T \\).\n   - From the figure, one full cycle takes 20 ms, so \\( T = 20 \\times 10^{-3} \\) s.\n   - Therefore, \\( \\omega = 2\\pi / (20 \\times 10^{-3}) = 314 \\, \\text{rad/s} \\).\n   - This option is correct.\n\n3. **Option C: Initial phase is 60 \u00b0.**\n   - The initial phase does not appear to be 60\u00b0, as the waveform does not exhibit a phase shift noticeable from the vertical axis. \n   - This option is incorrect.\n\n4. **Option D: The cycle is (20-5) ms.**\n   - The cycle period is the full time for one waveform, which is clearly labelled as 20 ms.\n   - Hence, the complete cycle is not (20-5) ms.\n   - This option is incorrect.\n\nANSWER: B."
"To determine the relationship between the calculated (P Principle) and measured (P Real) lateral earth pressures for the two different support structures, we need to consider the nature of the support systems:\n\n1. **Cantilever Support Structure**:\n   - The cantilever support relies solely on the bending stiffness of the piles to resist the lateral earth pressure.\n   - Typically, this would involve greater deflection and higher measured lateral pressures due to lack of additional support to counteract soil pressure effectively.\n\n2. **Internal Support Structure**:\n   - This structure provides additional rigidity and resistance against lateral forces through internal bracing.\n   - It reduces wall deflection and typically results in lower measured lateral pressures compared to the cantilever support.\n\n**Analyzing the Options**:\n- **P Principle 1 = P Principle 2**: Both support systems are subjected to the same theoretical lateral Rankine soil pressure since the geological conditions and depth are identical.\n  \n- **P Real 1 < P Real 2**: The cantilever structure (System 1) is expected to show higher measured pressures due to greater deflection. Lower deflection in the internally supported structure (System 2) leads to reduced measured pressure.\n\nTherefore, **option A** reflects these considerations correctly:\n\nANSWER: A."
