"To determine which aspect a modern art critic would be least likely to criticize in Hogarth's work:\n\nA. Emphasis on traditional portrayals of humans - Hogarth\u2019s work often broke away from traditional depictions by including more lively and realistic scenes of everyday life.\n\nB. Use of stereotyped characters - Hogarth frequently employed stereotyped characters to convey social messages and satire.\n\nC. Attention to realistic detail - Hogarth is known for his intricate attention to detail, which is often celebrated rather than criticized.\n\nD. Typical portraiture composition - Hogarth\u2019s compositions often deviated from typical portraiture, focusing instead on complex scenes and narratives.\n\nANSWER: C."
