"To determine which term refers to the part of a story that follows the climax and includes events after the character changes, we can analyze each option:\n\nA. Climax - This is the point of greatest tension in the story, where the main conflict reaches its peak. It is not the part that occurs after the climax.\n\nB. Resolution - This refers to the conclusion of the story, where conflicts are resolved and the story comes to an end. It follows after the events that occur once the climax has been resolved.\n\nC. Rising Action - This includes events that build up to the climax, increasing tension and developing the conflict. It is not after the climax.\n\nD. Falling Action - This is the part of the story that follows the climax, where the tension starts to decrease, and events lead towards the resolution. It encompasses events after the character changes.\n\nThe correct answer is the term that refers to the part of the story after the climax and before the resolution.\n\nANSWER: D. Falling Action."
