"To determine the before-tax income, we need to create a contribution margin income statement. \n\n1. **Calculate Total Sales:**\n   - Total Sales = Sales Price per Hat \u00d7 Number of Hats Sold\n   - Total Sales = $80 \u00d7 22,000 = $1,760,000\n\n2. **Calculate Total Variable Costs:**\n   - Total Variable Cost per Hat = $55\n   - Total Variable Costs = Total Variable Cost per Hat \u00d7 Number of Hats Sold\n   - Total Variable Costs = $55 \u00d7 22,000 = $1,210,000\n\n3. **Calculate Contribution Margin:**\n   - Contribution Margin = Total Sales - Total Variable Costs\n   - Contribution Margin = $1,760,000 - $1,210,000 = $550,000\n\n4. **Subtract Fixed Expenses to Find Before-Tax Income:**\n   - Fixed Expenses = $500,000\n   - Before-Tax Income = Contribution Margin - Fixed Expenses\n   - Before-Tax Income = $550,000 - $500,000 = $50,000\n\nThe before-tax income is $50,000.\n\nANSWER: A"
"To calculate the cost of tax returns in process as of March 31 using the FIFO method, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the Equivalent Units of Production (EUP) for Conversion Costs:**\n\n   - Returns in process at March 1: 100 returns (30% complete)\n   - Returns started and completed in March: 1,600 - 200 = 1,400 returns\n   - Returns in process at March 31: 200 returns (90% complete)\n\n   EUP for returns in process at March 31 = 200 returns \u00d7 90% = 180 units\n\n2. **Calculate the Total Conversion Costs:**\n\n   - Beginning Conversion Costs (March 1): $2,500\n   - Additional Conversion Costs During March: $173,250\n\n   Total Conversion Costs = $2,500 + $173,250 = $175,750\n\n3. **Determine the Cost per Equivalent Unit:**\n\n   Total equivalent units for conversion:\n   \n   - March 1 to March 31:\n     - Completed: 100 returns \u00d7 (100% - 30%) = 70 units\n     - Started and completed in March: 1,400 units\n     - In process on March 31: 180 units\n   \n   Total EUP for conversion = 70 + 1,400 + 180 = 1,650 units\n\n   Cost per equivalent unit for conversion = Total Conversion Costs / Total EUP for conversion\n   = $175,750 / 1,650 \n\n4. **Calculate the Cost of Tax Returns in Process as of March 31:**\n\n   Cost of returns in process at March 31 = EUP for March 31 returns \u00d7 Cost per equivalent unit\n   = 180 units \u00d7 ($175,750 / 1,650)\n\n   \u2248 $19,180\n\nANSWER: B. $19,180"
