"To find the total variable cost at the breakeven point, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the breakeven point**: This is where total revenue equals total cost on the graph. From the graph, this occurs at 20,000 units.\n\n2. **Identify the total cost and fixed cost at breakeven**, which is also the total revenue at the breakeven point:\n   - At 20,000 units, the total cost is $60,000.\n   - Fixed costs are $20,000 (this is constant and indicated by the horizontal line).\n\n3. **Calculate the total variable cost**:\n   - Total cost = Fixed costs + Total variable cost\n   - $60,000 = $20,000 + Total variable cost\n   - Total variable cost = $60,000 - $20,000 = $40,000\n\nThus, the total variable cost at the breakeven point is $40,000.\n\nANSWER: B"
