"To calculate the cost of completed tax returns for the month of March using the FIFO method, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Determine the Equivalent Units of Production (EUP) for Conversion Costs:**\n\n    - **Beginning Work in Process (WIP):** 100 returns, 30% complete initially. So, 70% of the work is needed to complete these returns.\n    - **Started and Completed during March:** 1,400 returns (1,600 returns started - 200 returns in process at the end of the period).\n    - **Ending WIP:** 200 returns, 90% complete. So, only 10% needs completion.\n\n   Calculate EUP:\n   \\[\n   \\text{EUP for beginning WIP} = 100 \\times 70\\% = 70\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{EUP for started and completed} = 1,400\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{EUP for ending WIP} = 200 \\times 10\\% = 20\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total EUP for March} = 70 + 1,400 + 20 = 1,490\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the Conversion Cost per Unit:**\n\n   - Total conversion costs:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Beginning WIP cost} = \\$2,500\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\text{Cost incurred in March} = \\$173,250\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\text{Total conversion costs} = \\$2,500 + \\$173,250 = \\$175,750\n     \\]\n   - Cost per equivalent unit:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Cost per EUP} = \\frac{\\text{Total conversion costs}}{\\text{Total EUP}} = \\frac{\\$175,750}{1,490} \\approx \\$118 \\text{ per unit}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the Cost of Goods Completed and Transferred Out:**\n\n\\[\n\\text{Cost of Goods Completed} = (\\text{EUP for beginning WIP} + \\text{EUP for started and completed}) \\times \\text{Cost per EUP}\n\\]\n\\[\n= (70 + 1,400) \\times \\$118 = 1,470 \\times \\$118 = \\$173,460\n\\]\n\nANSWER: C"
