"To determine whether the largest year-to-year increase in the unemployment rate occurred from June 2008 to June 2009, we need to compare the unemployment rates for June in each consecutive year from 2002 to 2011 and calculate the differences.\n\n1. **June 2002 to June 2003**: 5.8% to 6.3% = 0.5% increase\n2. **June 2003 to June 2004**: 6.3% to 5.6% = 0.7% decrease\n3. **June 2004 to June 2005**: 5.6% to 5.0% = 0.6% decrease\n4. **June 2005 to June 2006**: 5.0% to 4.6% = 0.4% decrease\n5. **June 2006 to June 2007**: 4.6% to 4.5% = 0.1% decrease\n6. **June 2007 to June 2008**: 4.5% to 5.6% = 1.1% increase\n7. **June 2008 to June 2009**: 5.6% to 9.5% = 3.9% increase\n8. **June 2009 to June 2010**: 9.5% to 9.6% = 0.1% increase\n9. **June 2010 to June 2011**: 9.6% to 9.1% = 0.5% decrease\n\nThe largest increase, 3.9%, indeed occurred from June 2008 to June 2009. \n\nANSWER: A. True."
