"To calculate the project variance, we need to focus on the critical path, which is the sequence of activities with zero slack. From the table, activities A, C, E, and G form the critical path since they all have slack = 0.\n\nWe'll sum up the variances of the activities on the critical path:\n\n- Activity A variance: \\( \\frac{2}{6} \\)\n- Activity C variance: \\( \\frac{4}{6} \\)\n- Activity E variance: \\( \\frac{2}{6} \\)\n- Activity G variance: \\( \\frac{1}{6} \\)\n\nNow, add these variances together:\n\n\\[ \\text{Total Variance} = \\frac{2}{6} + \\frac{4}{6} + \\frac{2}{6} + \\frac{1}{6} = \\frac{9}{6} = 1.5 \\]\n\nANSWER: B"
