"To find the percentage increase in sales for A.B.C. Corp. from 1965 to 1966:\n\n1. Identify sales figures:\n   - 1966 sales = $10,000,000\n   - 1965 sales = $8,000,000\n\n2. Calculate the increase in sales:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Increase} = \\text{Sales in 1966} - \\text{Sales in 1965} = 10,000,000 - 8,000,000 = 2,000,000\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate the percentage increase:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Percentage Increase} = \\left(\\frac{\\text{Increase}}{\\text{Sales in 1965}}\\right) \\times 100 = \\left(\\frac{2,000,000}{8,000,000}\\right) \\times 100 = 25\\%\n   \\]\n\nANSWER: 25%"
