"To solve this problem, we need to calculate the sample mean and the sample standard deviation from the given data.\n\n### Step 1: Calculate the Sample Mean\n\nSum up all the data values and divide by the number of values.\n\n\\[\n\\text{Sum} = 0.5 + 1.75 + 2 + 2.25 + 2.25 + 2.5 + 2.75 + 3.25 + 3.75 + 3.75 + 4.25 + 4.25 + 4.25 + 4.25 + 4.5 + 4.75 + 4.75 + 4.75 + 5 + 5 + 5.25 + 5.25 + 5.5 + 5.5 + 5.5 + 5.75 + 5.75 + 6 + 6 + 6 + 6.25 + 6.25 + 6.5 + 6.5 + 6.5 + 6.75 + 6.75 + 6.75 + 7.25 + 7.25 + 7.25 + 7.75 + 8 + 8.25 + 9.5 + 9.5 + 9.75 + 10.75 \n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total number of values} = 49 \n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{Mean} = \\frac{\\text{Sum}}{49}\n\\]\n\nCalculating this, you get:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Mean} \\approx 5.51\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Calculate the Sample Standard Deviation\n\n1. Calculate each data point's deviation from the mean, square it, sum these squares.\n2. Divide by the number of samples minus 1, then take the square root.\n\n\\[\n\\text{Variance} = \\frac{1}{49 - 1}\\sum (x_i - \\text{Mean})^2\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{Standard deviation} = \\sqrt{\\text{Variance}}\n\\]\n\nDoing the calculations, you get:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Standard deviation} \\approx 2.15\n\\]\n\n### Conclusion\nThe distribution of \\( X \\) can be approximated as \\( X \\sim N(5.51, 2.15) \\).\n\nANSWER: B"
