"To calculate the degrees of freedom (df) for a contingency table, you use the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{df} = (r - 1) \\times (c - 1) \\]\n\nwhere \\( r \\) is the number of rows, and \\( c \\) is the number of columns.\n\nFrom the table:\n- There are 4 rows (for family sizes: 1, 2, 3\u20134, 5+).\n- There are 4 columns (for car sizes: Sub & Compact, Mid-size, Full-size, Van & Truck).\n\nPlug these values into the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{df} = (4 - 1) \\times (4 - 1) = 3 \\times 3 = 9 \\]\n\nANSWER: C."
