"To construct a 95% confidence interval for the true mean number of colors on national flags, we follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the Sample Mean (\\(\\bar{X}\\)):**\n\n   \\[\n   \\bar{X} = \\frac{\\sum (X \\times \\text{Freq})}{\\sum \\text{Freq}} = \\frac{(1 \\times 1) + (2 \\times 7) + (3 \\times 18) + (4 \\times 7) + (5 \\times 6)}{39}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = \\frac{1 + 14 + 54 + 28 + 30}{39} = \\frac{127}{39} \\approx 3.26\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the Sample Standard Deviation (\\(s\\)):**\n\n   \\[\n   s = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\sum ((X - \\bar{X})^2 \\times \\text{Freq})}{n-1}}\n   \\]\n   First, calculate \\((X - \\bar{X})^2 \\times \\text{Freq}\\) for each X:\n   - For \\(X=1\\): \\((1 - 3.26)^2 \\times 1 = 5.12\\)\n   - For \\(X=2\\): \\((2 - 3.26)^2 \\times 7 = 11.08\\)\n   - For \\(X=3\\): \\((3 - 3.26)^2 \\times 18 = 1.35\\)\n   - For \\(X=4\\): \\((4 - 3.26)^2 \\times 7 = 3.75\\)\n   - For \\(X=5\\): \\((5 - 3.26)^2 \\times 6 = 15.40\\)\n\n   \\[\n   \\sum = 5.12 + 11.08 + 1.35 + 3.75 + 15.40 = 36.70\n   \\]\n\n   \\[\n   s = \\sqrt{\\frac{36.70}{39-1}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{36.70}{38}} \\approx 0.98\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the Standard Error (\\(SE\\)):**\n\n   \\[\n   SE = \\frac{s}{\\sqrt{n}} = \\frac{0.98}{\\sqrt{39}} \\approx 0.157\n   \\]\n\n4. **Find the \\(t\\)-value for 95% Confidence Interval:**\n\n   For a 95% confidence interval and \\(n-1 = 38\\) degrees of freedom, we typically use a \\(t\\)-table to find the \\(t\\)-value. The area in each tail for a 95% confidence interval is 0.025 (B).\n\n5. **Construct the Confidence Interval:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\text{Margin of Error} = t \\times SE \\approx 2.024 \\times 0.157 \\approx 0.318\n   \\]\n   (Use \\(t\\)-value \u2248 2.024 for 38 df from the \\(t\\)-table)\n\n   \\[\n   \\text{Confidence Interval} = (\\bar{X} - \\text{Margin of Error}, \\bar{X} + \\text{Margin of Error}) = (3.26 - 0.318, 3.26 + 0.318) = (2.94, 3.58)\n   \\]\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nThe area in each tail of the 95% confidence interval is **0.025**.\n\nANSWER: B."
