"To determine the forces and moment at section C, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Free Body Diagram (FBD) Setup**:\n    - The beam is in static equilibrium, with point A being a pin connection and point B where the cable is attached to the wall.\n    - The distance from A to the point of force application is 0.75 m, and the same distance from A to C.\n  \n2. **Identify Forces**:\n    - The force at P=8 kN is vertical.\n    - The reaction forces at A: \\( A_x \\) and \\( A_y \\).\n    - The tension in the cable acts horizontally at B.\n\n3. **Calculate Reaction Forces at A**:\n    - Sum of moments about A \\( \\Sigma M_A = 0 \\):\n        - Consider moments created by \\( P \\) and the tension via the pulley.\n        - \\( M_A = P \\times 0.75 \\) m.\n        - Assuming \\( T \\) (tension in the cable) bypasses pulley and acts horizontally.\n        - \\( 8 \\times 0.75 = T \\times (1.5 + 0.1) \\)\n        - \\( 6 = T \\times 1.6 \\)\n        - \\( T = \\frac{6}{1.6} = 3.75 \\, \\text{kN} \\).\n\n    - Sum of forces in the horizontal \\( \\Sigma F_x = 0 \\):\n        - \\( A_x = T = 3.75 \\, \\text{kN} \\).\n\n    - Sum of forces in the vertical \\( \\Sigma F_y = 0 \\):\n        - \\( A_y + T_v - P = 0 \\)\n        - Tension vertically at pulley: \\( T_v = \\frac{0.1}{0.5} \\times 3.75 \\).\n        - \\( A_y = 8 - 0.75 \\times 3.75 \\).\n\n4. **Internal Forces at Section C**:\n    - **Normal Force (\\( N_C \\))**: Acts horizontally, \\( N_C = -A_x = -3.75 \\, \\text{kN} \\).\n    - **Shear Force (\\( V_C \\))**: Acts vertically, \\( V_C = -P = -8 \\, \\text{kN} \\).\n    - **Moment (\\( M_C \\))**: Moment due to \\( P \\) at C,\n        - \\( M_C = P \\times 0.75 = 8 \\times 0.75 = 6 \\, \\text{kN}\\cdot\\text{m} \\).\n\nReviewing the calculations for errors:\n\n5. **Checking with Given Options**:\n    - None of the initial tension calculations fit; upon revisiting basic assumptions:\n    - Update based on simplification for \\( \\Sigma M_A \\) realizing there's a mist