\nANSWER: A."
"To find the force \\( P \\) that causes a tilt of 0.015\u00b0, we need to consider the deformation of the wires due to the applied force.\n\n### Step-by-Step Reasoning:\n\n1. **Material Properties:**\n   - 304 stainless steel has a modulus of elasticity \\( E \\approx 28,000 \\) ksi.\n\n2. **Wire Details:**\n   - Diameter \\( d = \\frac{1}{2} \\) in.\n   - Length \\( L = 2 \\) ft = 24 in.\n\n   Calculate the cross-sectional area \\( A \\):\n   \\[\n   A = \\frac{\\pi d^2}{4} = \\frac{\\pi (0.5)^2}{4} \\approx 0.1963 \\, \\text{in}^2\n   \\]\n\n3. **Tilting Mechanism:**\n   - The beam will tilt around point \\( B \\) when force \\( P \\) is applied.\n   - The deformation \\( \\delta \\) in the wire \\( AD \\) can be related to the angle of tilt \\( \\theta \\) in radians:\n   \\[\n   \\theta = 0.015\u00b0 = 0.015 \\times \\frac{\\pi}{180} \\, \\text{radians} \\approx 0.0002618 \\, \\text{radians}\n   \\]\n   - At point \\( A \\), the horizontal distance due to tilt is \\( L \\times \\theta \\).\n\n4. **Deformation Calculation:**\n   \\[\n   \\delta = L \\times \\theta = 24 \\times 0.0002618 \\approx 0.006283 \\, \\text{in}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Force in Wire:**\n   Using the formula for deformation \\( \\delta = \\frac{PL}{AE} \\), solve for \\( P \\):\n   \\[\n   P = \\frac{\\delta \\cdot AE}{L} = \\frac{0.006283 \\cdot 0.1963 \\cdot 28000}{24}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   P \\approx 6.48 \\, \\text{kip}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the correct force \\( P \\) is closest to option B.\n\nANSWER: B. 6.48 kip."
