"To find the factor of safety against bearing failure for the concrete under the plate at C, we need to calculate the bearing stress and compare it to the failure stress.\n\n1. **Determine Total Load on Support A (Pin Support C):**\n   - Sum of vertical forces to the left of C: 150 kip (at A) + (300 kip * 2 sections) = 750 kip\n\n   The load supported by A is 750 kip.\n\n2. **Calculate the Area of the Bearing Plate:**\n   - Bearing plate dimension = 21 in. x 21 in.\n   - Area = \\( 21 \\, \\text{in} \\times 21 \\, \\text{in} = 441 \\, \\text{in}^2 \\)\n\n3. **Calculate Bearing Stress:**\n   - Bearing stress (\u03c3_b) = Total load / Area \n   - \\( \\sigma_b = \\frac{750 \\, \\text{kip}}{441 \\, \\text{in}^2} \\)\n   - Convert kips to pounds: \\( 750 \\, \\text{kip} = 750,000 \\, \\text{lb} \\)\n   - \\( \\sigma_b = \\frac{750,000 \\, \\text{lb}}{441 \\, \\text{in}^2} \\approx 1701.4 \\, \\text{psi} \\)\n   - Convert psi to ksi: \\( 1701.4 \\, \\text{psi} = 1.7014 \\, \\text{ksi} \\)\n\n4. **Calculate Factor of Safety:**\n   - \\( \\text{Factor of Safety} = \\frac{\\text{Failure Stress}}{\\text{Bearing Stress}} \\)\n   - \\( \\text{Factor of Safety} = \\frac{4 \\, \\text{ksi}}{1.7014 \\, \\text{ksi}} \\approx 2.35 \\)\n\n5. **Determine the Closest Option:**\n   - The closest factor of safety from the given options is 2.30.\n\n**ANSWER: A.**"
