"To solve this problem, we need to determine the average normal stress and shear stress on the inclined plane, as well as the normal stress on the cross section.\n\n### Known quantities:\n- Axial load \\( P = 19.80 \\, \\text{kip} = 19,800 \\, \\text{lb} \\)\n- Diameter of the specimen \\( d = 0.5 \\, \\text{in.} \\)\n- Failure angle \\( \\theta = 52^\\circ \\)\n\n### Calculations:\n\n1. **Cross-sectional area:**\n   \\[\n   A = \\frac{\\pi}{4} d^2 = \\frac{\\pi}{4} (0.5)^2 = 0.19635 \\, \\text{in}^2\n   \\]\n\n2. **Average normal stress on the cross section:**\n   \\[\n   \\sigma_{\\text{avg}} = \\frac{P}{A} = \\frac{19,800}{0.19635} = 100,858.38 \\, \\text{psi} = 100.858 \\, \\text{ksi}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Inclined plane area:**\n   The area of the inclined plane \\( A_{\\text{inc}} \\) can be calculated using the angle:\n   \\[\n   A_{\\text{inc}} = \\frac{A}{\\cos \\theta} = \\frac{0.19635}{\\cos 52^\\circ} = 0.31819 \\, \\text{in}^2\n   \\]\n\n4. **Average normal stress on inclined plane:**\n   \\[\n   \\sigma_{\\text{avg,inc}} = \\frac{P \\cos^2 \\theta}{A} = \\frac{19,800 \\cos^2 52^\\circ}{0.19635} = 61.663 \\, \\text{ksi}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Average shear stress on inclined plane:**\n   \\[\n   \\tau_{\\text{avg,inc}} = \\frac{P \\sin \\theta \\cos \\theta}{A} = \\frac{19,800 \\sin 52^\\circ \\cos 52^\\circ}{0.19635} = 48.956 \\, \\text{ksi}\n   \\]\n\n### Conclusion:\n\nMatching the calculated values with the options provided:\n\n- \\(\\sigma_{\\text{avg,inc}} = 61.663 \\, \\text{ksi}\\)\n- \\(\\tau_{\\text{avg,inc}} = 48.956 \\, \\text{ksi}\\)\n- \\(\\sigma_{\\text{avg}} = 108.841 \\, \\text{ksi}\\)\n\nThe correct option is:\nANSWER: A"
