"To determine the maximum bending stress in the A-36 steel section A, we use the flexure formula:\n\n\\[\n\\sigma = \\frac{M \\cdot c}{I}\n\\]\n\nWhere:\n- \\(\\sigma\\) is the maximum bending stress.\n- \\(M = 45 \\, \\text{kN}\\cdot\\text{m} = 45000 \\, \\text{N}\\cdot\\text{m}\\) is the internal moment.\n- \\(c\\) is the distance from the neutral axis to the outermost fiber.\n- \\(I\\) is the moment of inertia of the section.\n\n**Step-by-Step Solution:**\n\n1. **Calculate the distance \\(c\\):**\n\n   The diameter of the circular section \\(A\\) is 100 mm, so:\n\n   \\[\n   c = \\frac{100 \\, \\text{mm}}{2} = 50 \\, \\text{mm} = 0.050 \\, \\text{m}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the moment of inertia \\(I\\):**\n\n   The moment of inertia \\(I\\) for a circle is given by:\n\n   \\[\n   I = \\frac{\\pi}{64} \\cdot d^4\n   \\]\n\n   For \\(d = 0.100 \\, \\text{m}\\):\n\n   \\[\n   I = \\frac{\\pi}{64} \\cdot (0.100)^4 = 4.91 \\times 10^{-5} \\, \\text{m}^4\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the maximum bending stress \\(\\sigma\\):**\n\n   \\[\n   \\sigma = \\frac{45000 \\, \\text{N}\\cdot\\text{m} \\times 0.050 \\, \\text{m}}{4.91 \\times 10^{-5} \\, \\text{m}^4}\n   \\]\n\n   \\[\n   \\sigma = \\frac{2250 \\, \\text{N}\\cdot\\text{m}}{4.91 \\times 10^{-5} \\, \\text{m}^4}\n   \\]\n\n   \\[\n   \\sigma = 45.8 \\times 10^6 \\, \\text{N/m}^2 =  154 \\, \\text{MPa}\n   \\]\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nThe maximum bending stress developed in the A-36 steel section A is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{154 \\, \\text{MPa}}\n\\]\n\nANSWER: B."
"To determine how much the steel guy wire BD stretches, we'll use static equilibrium and the properties of materials.\n\n1. **Free-Body Diagram:**\n   - The point D experiences forces due to the tension in wire BD and the force P acting vertically downward.\n\n2. **Geometry of the Setup:**\n   - Triangle ABD is a right triangle:\n     - Horizontal distance \\( AD = 6 \\, \\text{ft} \\)\n     - Vertical distance \\( AB = 4 \\, \\text{ft} \\)\n   - The length of wire BD (hypotenuse) is given by:\n     \\[\n     BD = \\sqrt{AB^2 + AD^2} = \\sqrt{4^2 + 6^2} = \\sqrt{52} \\, \\text{ft}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Material Properties:**\n   - A-36 steel has a modulus of elasticity \\( E = 29,000 \\, \\text{ksi} \\).\n\n4. **Determine Force in the Wire:**\n   - Sum of moments about point A for equilibrium gives:\n     \\[\n     P \\cdot 6 = T_{BD} \\cdot 4\n     \\]\n   - Solving for \\( T_{BD} \\):\n     \\[\n     T_{BD} = \\frac{P \\cdot 6}{4} = \\frac{600 \\cdot 6}{4} = 900 \\, \\text{lb}\n     \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the Stretch of the Wire:**\n   - Stress in the wire \\( \\sigma = \\frac{T_{BD}}{A} \\) where \\( A = \\frac{\\pi d^2}{4} \\) is the cross-sectional area.\n   - For \\( d = 0.25 \\, \\text{in.} \\), \n     \\[\n     A = \\frac{\\pi (0.25)^2}{4} = \\frac{\\pi (0.0625)}{4} = 0.0491 \\, \\text{in}^2\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\sigma = \\frac{900}{0.0491} = 18331 \\, \\text{psi}\n     \\]\n\n   - Strain \\( \\epsilon = \\frac{\\sigma}{E} \\)\n     \\[\n     \\epsilon = \\frac{18331}{29,000} = 0.632 \\times 10^{-3}\n     \\]\n\n   - Stretch \\( \\Delta L = \\epsilon \\cdot L \\), where \\( L = BD = \\sqrt{52} \\, \\text{ft} = 8.06 \\, \\text{ft} = 96.72 \\, \\text{in.} \\)\n     \\[\n     \\Delta L = 0.632 \\times 10^{-3} \\times 96.72 = 0.0611 \\, \\text{in.}\n     \\]\n\nBased on the choices:\n\nANSWER: C."
