"To find the initial permeability and initial relative permeability, we'll use the first portion of the data where the values of H (magnetic field strength) and B (magnetic flux density) begin to increase from zero.\n\n### Initial Permeability Calculation\n1. Use the first available non-zero values:\n   - \\( H = 10 \\, \\text{A/m} \\)\n   - \\( B = 0.03 \\, \\text{tesla} \\)\n\n2. Apply the formula for permeability (\\( \\mu \\)):\n   \\[\n   \\mu = \\frac{B}{H}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\mu = \\frac{0.03}{10} = 0.003 \\, \\text{tesla meter/ampere} = 0.003 \\, \\text{henry/meter}\n   \\]\n\n### Initial Relative Permeability Calculation\n1. Calculate the relative permeability (\\( \\mu_r \\)) using:\n   \\[\n   \\mu_r = \\frac{\\mu}{\\mu_0}\n   \\]\n   where \\( \\mu_0 = 4\\pi \\times 10^{-7} \\, \\text{henry/meter} \\).\n\n2. Substitute the values:\n   \\[\n   \\mu_r = \\frac{0.003}{4\\pi \\times 10^{-7}}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\mu_r \\approx \\frac{0.003}{1.25664 \\times 10^{-6}} \\approx 2387\n   \\]\n\nThe initial relative permeability is approximately 2387, which corresponds to option B.\n\nANSWER: B."
