suggests typo in calculation. Correct form under standard bolt circumstances:\n\n**Select the most appropriate choice from options provided:**\n\nANSWER: A. \\( \\tau = 5658\\ \\text{psi} \\)"
"To determine the axial force \\( P \\) applied to the specimen, we can use the formula for normal stress:\n\n\\[\n\\sigma = \\frac{P}{A}\n\\]\n\nwhere \\( \\sigma = 2 \\text{ ksi} \\) (the average normal stress), \\( P \\) is the axial force, and \\( A \\) is the cross-sectional area of the specimen.\n\nFrom the image, the cross-sectional area \\( A \\) is:\n\nWidth = 2 in (due to dimension 'a')\n\nThickness = 1 in\n\nSo, the area \\( A \\) = Width * Thickness = \\( 2 \\text{ in} \\times 1 \\text{ in} = 2 \\text{ in}^2 \\).\n\nNow, substituting in the stress formula:\n\n\\[\n2 \\text{ ksi} = \\frac{P}{2 \\text{ in}^2}\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( P \\):\n\n\\[\nP = 2 \\text{ ksi} \\times 2 \\text{ in}^2 = 4 \\text{ kips}\n\\]\n\nSo, the axial force applied to the specimen is \\( 4 \\text{ kips} \\).\n\nANSWER: B."
