"To determine the energy for defect formation, we'll use the Arrhenius equation for Schottky defects, which relates the number of defects \\( N_s \\) to temperature \\( T \\):\n\n\\[ N_s = N \\exp\\left(-\\frac{Q}{2kT}\\right) \\]\n\nWhere:\n- \\( N \\) is the number of atoms in the crystal.\n- \\( Q \\) is the energy for defect formation.\n- \\( k \\) is the Boltzmann constant (\\(8.617 \\times 10^{-5} \\, \\text{eV/K}\\)).\n- \\( T \\) is the temperature in Kelvin.\n\nTo find \\( N \\), we use the density formula: \n\n\\[ N = \\frac{\\rho \\times N_A}{M} \\]\n\nWhere:\n- \\( \\rho \\) is the density.\n- \\( N_A \\) is Avogadro's number (\\(6.022 \\times 10^{23} \\, \\text{atoms/mol}\\)).\n- \\( M \\) is the molar mass of the oxide ceramic.\n\nGiven:\n- At 750\u00b0C (1023 K), \\( N_s = 5.7 \\times 10^9 \\).\n- At 1500\u00b0C (1773 K), \\( N_s = 5.8 \\times 10^{17} \\).\n\nCalculate \\( N_1 \\) and \\( N_2 \\) using the densities and rearranging the Arrhenius equation for \\( Q \\):\n\n1. Rearrange the equation for two temperatures:\n   \n   \\[\n   \\frac{N_{s1}}{N_{s2}} = \\frac{N_1}{N_2} \\exp\\left(\\frac{Q(1/2k)(1/T_2 - 1/T_1)}\\right)\n   \\]\n\nSince \\( N \\) approximately remains the same at close temperatures, assume \\( N_1 \\approx N_2 \\):\n\n2. Solve for \\( Q \\):\n\nUsing given density at 750\u00b0C and 1500\u00b0C:\n- At 750\u00b0C: \\(\\rho_1 = 3.50 \\, \\text{g/cm}^3\\)\n- At 1500\u00b0C: \\(\\rho_2 = 3.40 \\, \\text{g/cm}^3\\)\n\nThe molar mass \\( M \\) also remains constant for the same substance.\n\nSubstitute all values and calculate \\( Q \\).\n\n\\[ \\ln\\left(\\frac{5.7 \\times 10^9}{5.8 \\times 10^{17}}\\right) \\approx -\\frac{Q}{2k} \\left(\\frac{1}{1773} - \\frac{1}{1023}\\right) \\]\n\nSolve numerically for \\( Q \\) using these known values:\n\n- Calculate \\( \\Delta \\left(\\frac{1}{T}\\right) \\):\n  \\[\n  \\frac{1}{1023} - \\frac{1}{1773} \\approx 0.00035 \\, \\text{K}^{-1}\n  \\]\n\n- Calculate \\( \\ln\\left(\\frac{5.7 \\times 10^9}{5.8 \\times 10^{17}}\\right) \\) approximately:\n  \\[\n  \\approx -18.5\n  \\]\n\n- Solve for \\( Q \\):\n  \\[\n  -18.5 \\approx -\\frac{Q}{2 \\times 8.617 \\times 10^{-5}} \\times 0.00035\n  \\]\n\n  \\[\n  Q \\approx 7.70 \\, \\text{eV}\n  \\]\n\nANSWER: A"
