"To determine the force \\( P \\) applied to the plate, we need to integrate the stress distribution over the area of contact to find the total force.\n\nGiven stress distribution:\n\\[\n\\sigma(x) = 15x^{1/2} \\text{ MPa}\n\\]\n\nThe stress varies linearly up to 30 MPa at the end. We assume the distribution is over a width of \\( x = 4 \\, \\text{m} \\).\n\n1. **Integration of Stress over Area:**\n\n   The width of the plate is \\( w = 0.5 \\, \\text{m} \\).\n   \n   The differential force \\( dF \\) is given by:\n   \\[\n   dF = \\sigma(x) \\times w \\times dx = 15x^{1/2} \\times 0.5 \\times dx\n   \\]\n\n2. **Integrate over the length**:\n\n   \\[\n   F = \\int_{0}^{4} 15x^{1/2} \\times 0.5 \\, dx\n   \\]\n\n   \\[\n   F = 7.5 \\int_{0}^{4} x^{1/2} \\, dx\n   \\]\n\n   The integral of \\( x^{1/2} \\) is:\n   \\[\n   \\int x^{1/2} \\, dx = \\frac{2}{3} x^{3/2}\n   \\]\n\n   Evaluating the integral from 0 to 4:\n   \\[\n   F = 7.5 \\left[ \\frac{2}{3} x^{3/2} \\right]_{0}^{4}\n   \\]\n\n   \\[\n   F = 7.5 \\times \\frac{2}{3} \\times (4)^{3/2}\n   \\]\n\n   \\[\n   F = 7.5 \\times \\frac{2}{3} \\times 8\n   \\]\n\n   \\[\n   F = 7.5 \\times \\frac{16}{3}\n   \\]\n\n   \\[\n   F = 40 \\text{ MN}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the force \\( P \\) applied to the plate is 40 MN.\n\nANSWER: B"
