"To find the magnetic susceptibility (\\(\\chi_m\\)) corresponding to the maximum permeability (\\(\\mu\\)), we need to go through the following steps:\n\n1. **Find the Maximum Permeability**:  \n   The permeability (\\(\\mu\\)) is given by:\n   \\[\n   \\mu = \\frac{B}{H}\n   \\]\n   Calculate \\(\\mu\\) for each data point and identify the maximum value.\n\n2. **Calculate Magnetic Susceptibility**:  \n   The relationship between relative permeability (\\(\\mu_r\\)) and magnetic susceptibility (\\(\\chi_m\\)) is:\n   \\[\n   \\mu_r = \\chi_m + 1\n   \\]\n   Given that:\n   \\[\n   \\mu = \\mu_0 \\mu_r\n   \\]\n   Where \\(\\mu_0 = 4\\pi \\times 10^{-7} \\, \\text{T}\\cdot\\text{m/A}\\), solve for \\(\\chi_m\\).\n\n3. **Steps**:\n\n   Calculate \\(\\mu\\) for each \\((H, B)\\):\n   - \\((0, 0)\\): NA\n   - \\((10, 0.03)\\): \\(\\mu = \\frac{0.03}{10} = 0.003\\)\n   - \\((20, 0.07)\\): \\(\\mu = \\frac{0.07}{20} = 0.0035\\)\n   - \\((50, 0.23)\\): \\(\\mu = \\frac{0.23}{50} = 0.0046\\)\n   - \\((100, 0.70)\\): \\(\\mu = \\frac{0.70}{100} = 0.007\\)\n   - \\((150, 0.92)\\): \\(\\mu = \\frac{0.92}{150} = 0.00613\\)\n   - \\((200, 1.04)\\): \\(\\mu = \\frac{1.04}{200} = 0.0052\\)\n   - \\((400, 1.28)\\): \\(\\mu = \\frac{1.28}{400} = 0.0032\\)\n   - \\((600, 1.36)\\): \\(\\mu = \\frac{1.36}{600} = 0.00227\\)\n   - \\((800, 1.39)\\): \\(\\mu = \\frac{1.39}{800} = 0.0017375\\)\n   - \\((1000, 1.41)\\): \\(\\mu = \\frac{1.41}{1000} = 0.00141\\)\n\n   The maximum permeability is \\(0.007\\) for \\((H = 100, B = 0.70)\\).\n\n   Solve for \\(\\chi_m\\):\n   \\[\n   \\mu = \\mu_0 \\mu_r \\Rightarrow \\mu_r = \\frac{\\mu}{\\mu_0} = \\frac{0.007}{4\\pi \\times 10^{-7}} = 5575.276\n   \\]\n\n   \\[\n   \\chi_m = \\mu_r - 1 = 5575.276 - 1 \\approx 5574.276\n   \\]\n\nSince none of the options directly match \\(\\chi_m = 5574.276\\), check within the nearest possible answer:\n\nANSWER: B (7908)."
