"To solve this problem, we can use integration by parts. The formula for integration by parts is:\n\n\\[\n\\int u \\, dv = uv - \\int v \\, du\n\\]\n\nLet \\( u = f(x) \\) and \\( dv = g'(x) \\, dx \\), then \\( du = f'(x) \\, dx \\) and \\( v = g(x) \\).\n\nApplying integration by parts:\n\n\\[\n\\int_{-3}^{5} f(x) g'(x) \\, dx = f(x) g(x) \\big|_{-3}^{5} - \\int_{-3}^{5} f'(x) g(x) \\, dx\n\\]\n\nWe know from the problem: \n\n\\[\n\\int_{-3}^{5} f(x) g'(x) \\, dx = 9\n\\]\n\nNow evaluate \\( f(x)g(x) \\big|_{-3}^{5} \\):\n\n- At \\( x = 5 \\), \\( f(5) = 3 \\), \\( g(5) = 4 \\) so \\( f(5)g(5) = 3 \\times 4 = 12 \\)\n- At \\( x = -3 \\), \\( f(-3) = 2 \\), \\( g(-3) = -1 \\) so \\( f(-3)g(-3) = 2 \\times (-1) = -2 \\)\n\nThus, \n\n\\[\nf(x)g(x) \\big|_{-3}^{5} = 12 - (-2) = 14\n\\]\n\nUsing the integration by parts equation:\n\n\\[\n9 = 14 - \\int_{-3}^{5} f'(x) g(x) \\, dx\n\\]\n\nSolve for \\(\\int_{-3}^{5} f'(x) g(x) \\, dx\\):\n\n\\[\n\\int_{-3}^{5} f'(x) g(x) \\, dx = 14 - 9 = 5\n\\]\n\nThus, the answer is:\n\nANSWER: B."
