"To solve this problem, we need to use the properties of circles and arcs. Since chords \\( \\overline{AB} \\) and \\( \\overline{CD} \\) are parallel, the arcs cut off by these chords subtend an equal angle from the opposite side inside the circle.\n\nGiven:\n- \\(\\mathrm{m} \\overparen{AB} = 104^\\circ\\)\n- \\(\\mathrm{m} \\overparen{CD} = 168^\\circ\\)\n\nSince \\( \\overline{AB} \\) and \\( \\overline{CD} \\) are parallel, the arcs created by these chords are intercepted arcs. The total arc of the circle is \\(360^\\circ\\).\n\nTherefore, we calculate the arc \\( \\overparen{BD} \\):\n\n\\[ \n\\mathrm{m} \\overparen{BD} = 360^\\circ - (\\mathrm{m} \\overparen{AB} + \\mathrm{m} \\overparen{CD}) \n\\]\n\n\\[ \n\\mathrm{m} \\overparen{BD} = 360^\\circ - (104^\\circ + 168^\\circ) \n\\]\n\n\\[ \n\\mathrm{m} \\overparen{BD} = 360^\\circ - 272^\\circ \n\\]\n\n\\[ \n\\mathrm{m} \\overparen{BD} = 88^\\circ \n\\]\n\nThus, the measure of \\(\\mathrm{m} \\overparen{BD}\\) is \\(88^\\circ\\).\n\nANSWER: C."
