"To find the length of $\\overline{AC}$, we will use the fact that the tangents drawn from an external point to a circle are equal in length.\n\nGiven:\n- $AB = 20$\n- $AE = 12$\n- $CF = 15$\n\nLet's define some variables:\n- Let $AD = x$.\n- Since $AE = ED$ (tangents from the same point $A$), $ED = 12$.\n- Since $BF = BE$ (tangents from the same point $B$), $BE = 20 - 12 = 8$.\n- Since $CF = CD$ (tangents from the same point $C$), $CD = 15$.\n\nNow, for the tangent segments, we have:\n- $AD = AE = 12$\n- $BE = ED = 8$\n- $CF = CD = 15$\n\nWe need to find $AC$:\n- $AC = AD + DC = 12 + 15 = 27$.\n\nTherefore, the length of $\\overline{AC}$ is 27.\n\nANSWER: D."
