"To determine the maximum value of \\( f(\\vec{x}) = \\frac{1}{(x_1 - 1)^2 + (x_2 - 1)^2 + 1} \\) given the constraint \\( |x_i| \\leq \\frac{1}{2}, i = 1, 2 \\), we need to evaluate \\( f(\\vec{x}) \\) at the vertices of the square region defined by the constraints. These vertices are:\n\n1. \\( \\vec{x} = [0, 0] \\)\n2. \\( \\vec{x} = [\\frac{1}{2}, 0] \\)\n3. \\( \\vec{x} = [0, \\frac{1}{2}] \\)\n4. \\( \\vec{x} = [\\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{2}] \\)\n\nCalculate \\( f(\\vec{x}) \\) for each vertex:\n\n1. For \\( \\vec{x} = [0, 0] \\):\n   \\[\n   f([0, 0]) = \\frac{1}{(0 - 1)^2 + (0 - 1)^2 + 1} = \\frac{1}{1 + 1 + 1} = \\frac{1}{3}\n   \\]\n\n2. For \\( \\vec{x} = [\\frac{1}{2}, 0] \\):\n   \\[\n   f([\\frac{1}{2}, 0]) = \\frac{1}{(\\frac{1}{2} - 1)^2 + (0 - 1)^2 + 1} = \\frac{1}{\\frac{1}{4} + 1 + 1} = \\frac{1}{\\frac{9}{4}} = \\frac{4}{9}\n   \\]\n\n3. For \\( \\vec{x} = [0, \\frac{1}{2}] \\):\n   \\[\n   f([0, \\frac{1}{2}]) = \\frac{1}{(0 - 1)^2 + (\\frac{1}{2} - 1)^2 + 1} = \\frac{1}{1 + \\frac{1}{4} + 1} = \\frac{1}{\\frac{9}{4}} = \\frac{4}{9}\n   \\]\n\n4. For \\( \\vec{x} = [\\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{2}] \\):\n   \\[\n   f([\\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{2}]) = \\frac{1}{(\\frac{1}{2} - 1)^2 + (\\frac{1}{2} - 1)^2 + 1} = \\frac{1}{\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{4} + 1} = \\frac{1}{\\frac{3}{2}} = \\frac{2}{3}\n   \\]\n\nComparing these values, the maximum value of \\( f(\\vec{x}) \\) is \\( \\frac{2}{3} \\) at \\( \\vec{x} = [\\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{2}] \\).\n\nANSWER: D"
