"To determine which of the graphs is a Hamiltonian graph, we need to assess whether each graph contains a Hamiltonian cycle, which is a cycle that visits every vertex exactly once and returns to the starting vertex.\n\n**Graph (a):** \n\nVertices: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8  \n- Start at vertex 1: 1 \u2192 2 \u2192 3 \u2192 1 (cannot visit all vertices without revisiting some)  \n- Other paths also fail to visit all vertices without repetition.\n\nNo Hamiltonian cycle found.\n\n**Graph (b):**\n\nVertices: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8  \n- A possible Hamiltonian cycle: 1 \u2192 2 \u2192 3 \u2192 4 \u2192 7 \u2192 6 \u2192 8 \u2192 5 \u2192 1  \n- This path visits every vertex exactly once and returns to the starting vertex.\n\nGraph (b) has a Hamiltonian cycle.\n\nANSWER: B"
