"To find an approximation for \\( P'(7.5) \\), we use the values from the table near \\( t = 7.5 \\). We can use the average rate of change between \\( t = 6 \\) and \\( t = 9 \\) as the approximation:\n\n\\[\nP'(7.5) \\approx \\frac{P(9) - P(6)}{9 - 6} = \\frac{1040 - 760}{3} = \\frac{280}{3} = 93.333 \\, \\text{gallons/hr}^2\n\\]\n\nNow, to approximate the average value of the rate of fuel consumption on the interval \\( 12 \\leq t \\leq 24 \\) using a left Riemann sum with the four subintervals:\n\nThe subintervals are \\( [12, 15], [15, 18], [18, 21], [21, 24] \\).\n\n- For each subinterval, we take the value of \\( P(t) \\) at the left endpoint:\n  - \\( [12, 15] \\): \\( P(12) = 1200 \\)\n  - \\( [15, 18] \\): \\( P(15) = 1120 \\)\n  - \\( [18, 21] \\): \\( P(18) = 960 \\)\n  - \\( [21, 24] \\): \\( P(21) = 920 \\)\n\nCalculate the sum of these products:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Left Riemann sum} = (3)(1200) + (3)(1120) + (3)(960) + (3)(920) = 3600 + 3360 + 2880 + 2760 = 12600 \\, \\text{gallons}\n\\]\n\nThe interval length is \\( 12 \\) hours, so the average rate is:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Average value} = \\frac{12600}{12} = 1050 \\, \\text{gallons/hour}\n\\]\n\nCombining both parts:\n\nANSWER: A. 93.333; 1050."
"To solve this problem, let's start by defining the necessary variables and expressions.\n\n1. **Define Variables:**\n   - Let the radius of the large semicircle be \\( R \\).\n   - The diameter of the large semicircle is \\( 2R \\).\n\n2. **Small Semicircles:**\n   - Since \\( N \\) congruent semicircles lie on the diameter, each small semicircle has a diameter of \\( \\frac{2R}{N} \\).\n   - Therefore, the radius of each small semicircle is \\( \\frac{R}{N} \\).\n\n3. **Area of Small Semicircles (\\( A \\)):**\n   - The area of one small semicircle is:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{1}{2} \\pi \\left( \\frac{R}{N} \\right)^2 = \\frac{\\pi R^2}{2N^2}\n     \\]\n   - For \\( N \\) small semicircles, the combined area \\( A \\) is:\n     \\[\n     A = N \\times \\frac{\\pi R^2}{2N^2} = \\frac{\\pi R^2}{2N}\n     \\]\n\n4. **Area of Large Semicircle:**\n   - The area of the large semicircle is:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{1}{2} \\pi R^2\n     \\]\n\n5. **Area Outside Small Semicircles (\\( B \\)):**\n   - The area \\( B \\) is the area of the large semicircle minus the area of the small semicircles:\n     \\[\n     B = \\frac{1}{2} \\pi R^2 - \\frac{\\pi R^2}{2N} = \\frac{\\pi R^2}{2} \\left(1 - \\frac{1}{N}\\right)\n     \\]\n\n6. **Given Ratio \\( \\frac{A}{B} = \\frac{1}{18} \\):**\n   - Set up the equation:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{\\frac{\\pi R^2}{2N}}{\\frac{\\pi R^2}{2} \\left(1 - \\frac{1}{N}\\right)} = \\frac{1}{18}\n     \\]\n   - Simplify and solve for \\( N \\):\n     \\[\n     \\frac{1}{N \\left(1 - \\frac{1}{N}\\right)} = \\frac{1}{18}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\frac{1}{N - 1} = \\frac{1}{18}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     N - 1 = 18\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     N = 19\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:\n\nANSWER: D"
