"To determine the taper ratio, we need to calculate the reduction in diameter per unit length of the taper:\n\n1. **Initial Diameter (D1):** 18 units\n2. **Final Diameter (D2):** 14 units\n3. **Length of Taper (L):** 40 units (total length of the taper)\n\n**Taper ratio calculation:**\n\nThe taper ratio is calculated as the difference in diameters divided by the length of the taper:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Taper ratio} = \\frac{D1 - D2}{L} = \\frac{18 - 14}{40} = \\frac{4}{40} = \\frac{1}{10}\n\\]\n\nThus, the taper ratio is 1:10.\n\nANSWER: C."
