"To solve this problem, we need to determine two things: the distance traveled by the projectile when its speed has been reduced to one-half of the initial speed \\(v_0\\), and the terminal velocity of the projectile.\n\n1. **Equation of motion:**\n   The acceleration \\(a\\) is given by:\n   \\[\n   a = \\sigma - \\eta v^2\n   \\]\n   Using the chain rule, \\(a = v \\frac{dv}{dy}\\), we have:\n   \\[\n   v \\frac{dv}{dy} = \\sigma - \\eta v^2 \n   \\]\n   Rearranging terms gives:\n   \\[\n   v \\, dv = (\\sigma - \\eta v^2) \\, dy \n   \\]\n\n2. **Integration for distance:**\n   Separate variables and integrate from \\(v_0\\) to \\( \\frac{v_0}{2}\\) for velocity and from 0 to \\(y\\) for distance:\n   \\[\n   \\int_{v_0}^{v_0/2} \\frac{v}{\\sigma - \\eta v^2} \\, dv = \\int_0^y \\, dy\n   \\]\n   The integral on the left-hand side can be solved using partial fractions:\n   \\[\n   \\int \\frac{v}{\\sigma - \\eta v^2} \\, dv = -\\frac{1}{2\\eta} \\ln(\\sigma - \\eta v^2) + C \n   \\]\n   Evaluating from \\(v_0\\) to \\(\\frac{v_0}{2}\\),\n   \\[\n   -\\frac{1}{2\\eta} [\\ln(\\sigma - \\eta (\\frac{v_0}{2})^2) - \\ln(\\sigma - \\eta v_0^2)]\n   \\]\n   Simplifies to:\n   \\[\n   y = \\frac{1}{2\\eta} \\ln\\left(\\frac{\\sigma - \\eta v_0^2}{\\sigma - \\frac{\\eta v_0^2}{4}}\\right)\n   \\]\n\n3. **Terminal Velocity \\(v_t\\):**\n   Terminal velocity is reached when acceleration \\(a = 0\\), so:\n   \\[\n   \\sigma - \\eta v_t^2 = 0 \\implies v_t = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\sigma}{\\eta}}\n   \\]\n\n**Substituting Values:**\n- \\(\\sigma = 0.7 \\, \\text{m/s}^2\\)\n- \\(\\eta = 0.2 \\, \\text{m}^{-1}\\)\n- \\(v_0 = 4 \\, \\text{m/s}\\)\n\n- Calculate \\(y\\):\n  \\[\n  y = \\frac{1}{2 \\times 0.2} \\ln\\left(\\frac{0.7 - 0.2 \\times 4^2}{0.7 - 0.2 \\times \\left(\\frac{4}{2}\\right)^2}\\right) \n  \\]\n  \\[\n  y = \\frac{1}{0.4} \\ln\\left(\\frac{0.7 - 3.2}{0.7 - 1.6}\\right)\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  y = \\frac{1}{0.4} \\ln\\left(\\frac{-2.5}{-0.9}\\right)\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  y = \\frac{1}{0.4} \\ln\\left(2.7778\\right) \\approx 8.047 \\text{ m}\n  \\]\n\n- Calculate \\(v_t\\):\n  \\[\n  v_t = \\sqrt{\\frac{0.7}{0.2}} = \\sqrt{3.5} \\approx 1.871 \\, \\text{m/s}\n  \\]\n\nThus, the answer is:\n\nANSWER: C"
