"To solve this problem, we need to balance the chemical equation and perform stoichiometric calculations.\n\n### Balanced Equation:\n\\[ \\text{H}_2\\text{SO}_4 + 2\\text{NaOH} \\rightarrow \\text{Na}_2\\text{SO}_4 + 2\\text{H}_2\\text{O} \\]\n\n### Calculation Steps:\n\n1. **Moles of NaOH Given**: 0.75 mol\n\n2. **Stoichiometry**:\n   - From the balanced equation, 1 mole of H\\(_2\\)SO\\(_4\\) reacts with 2 moles of NaOH.\n   - So, 0.75 moles of NaOH will require:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Moles of H}_2\\text{SO}_4 = \\frac{0.75 \\text{ mol NaOH}}{2} = 0.375 \\text{ moles of H}_2\\text{SO}_4\n     \\]\n\n3. **Molar Mass of H\\(_2\\)SO\\(_4\\)**:\n   - H: 1.01 g/mol \u00d7 2 = 2.02 g/mol\n   - S: 32.07 g/mol\n   - O: 16.00 g/mol \u00d7 4 = 64.00 g/mol\n   - Total = 2.02 + 32.07 + 64.00 = 98.09 g/mol\n\n4. **Mass of H\\(_2\\)SO\\(_4\\) Required**:\n   - Use the formula: mass = moles \u00d7 molar mass\n   \\[\n   \\text{Mass of H}_2\\text{SO}_4 = 0.375 \\text{ mol} \\times 98.09 \\text{ g/mol} = 36.78375 \\text{ grams}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Round to Appropriate Significant Figures**:\n   - The calculated mass is approximately 36.78 grams.\n\n### Conclusion:\n\n- The closest answer choice is **C. 36.78 grams**.\n\nANSWER: C"
