"To find the percent by mass of water in cobalt(II) chloride hexahydrate, \\(\\text{CoCl}_2 \\cdot 6\\text{H}_2\\text{O}\\), we need to calculate the molar masses of the compound and its components:\n\n1. **Calculate the molar mass of \\(\\text{CoCl}_2\\):**\n\n   - Co: \\(1 \\times 58.93 \\, \\text{g/mol} = 58.93 \\, \\text{g/mol}\\)\n   - Cl: \\(2 \\times 35.45 \\, \\text{g/mol} = 70.90 \\, \\text{g/mol}\\)\n\n   \\(\\text{Molar mass of CoCl}_2 = 58.93 + 70.90 = 129.83 \\, \\text{g/mol}\\)\n\n2. **Calculate the molar mass of \\(6\\text{H}_2\\text{O}\\):**\n\n   - H: \\(2 \\times 1.01 \\, \\text{g/mol} = 2.02 \\, \\text{g/mol}\\)\n   - O: \\(1 \\times 16.00 \\, \\text{g/mol} = 16.00 \\, \\text{g/mol}\\)\n   - \\(\\text{H}_2\\text{O}: 2.02 + 16.00 = 18.02 \\, \\text{g/mol}\\)\n\n   \\(6 \\text{H}_2\\text{O}: 6 \\times 18.02 = 108.12 \\, \\text{g/mol}\\)\n\n3. **Calculate the molar mass of \\(\\text{CoCl}_2 \\cdot 6\\text{H}_2\\text{O}\\):**\n\n   \\(\\text{Molar mass of CoCl}_2 \\cdot 6\\text{H}_2\\text{O} = 129.83 + 108.12 = 237.95 \\, \\text{g/mol}\\)\n\n4. **Calculate the percent by mass of water:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\text{Percent by mass of water} = \\left(\\frac{108.12 \\, \\text{g/mol of water}}{237.95 \\, \\text{g/mol of hydrated compound}}\\right) \\times 100 = 45.44\\%\n   \\]\n\nANSWER: D"
