"To find the nonsense sequence, we need to understand which mRNA codon corresponds to a stop codon. Stop codons in mRNA are UAA, UAG, and UGA.\n\nThe DNA strand provided is:\n\n3'  A  T  A  T  _  _  T  T  T  _  _  _  _  _  _  _  _  _  _  _\n\nThis maps to the mRNA strand (transcription process: DNA sequence to mRNA sequence where A -> U, T -> A, C -> G, and G -> C):\n\n5'  U  A  U  A  _  _  A  A  A  _  _  _  _  _  _  _  _  _  _  _\n \nThe options given are DNA sequences. Let's transcribe them to mRNA:\n\nA. ACA -> UGU\nB. TCT -> AGA\nC. ACT -> UGA\nD. AGA -> UCU\n\nComparing with stop codons:\n\n- UGU: Not a stop codon\n- AGA: Not a stop codon\n- UGA: Stop codon\n- UCU: Not a stop codon\n\nThe nonsense codon is UGA, corresponding to the DNA sequence ACT.\n\nANSWER: C"
"To find the IUPAC and common names for the ether shown, we need to identify the alkyl and aryl groups connected to the oxygen atom.\n\n1. The structure has an oxygen (O) atom bonded to two groups.\n2. One group is a benzene ring, which is known as a phenyl group.\n3. The other group is an ethyl group (CH\u2082CH\u2083).\n\nTherefore, the ether is an ethyl group bonded to a phenyl group via the oxygen atom.\n\n- The IUPAC name of an ether is formed by listing the names of the groups on either side of the oxygen followed by 'ether'.\n- For the given molecule, the name becomes \"ethyl phenyl ether\".\n\nThe common name is also \"ethyl phenyl ether\".\n\nGiven the options:\nA. Ethyl methyl ether\nB. Ethyl phenyl ether\nC. Divinyl ether\nD. Diisopropyl ether\n\nThe correct answer is:\n\nANSWER: B."
"To identify the functional groups in each structural formula, we analyze the given structures:\n\n- **Structure A**: This structure shows a carbon (C) atom bonded to an OH group, characteristic of an alcohol group. Therefore, the functional group is A-OH.\n\n- **Structure B**: This structure has a carbon atom double-bonded to an oxygen (O) atom and single-bonded to another oxygen atom which is also bonded to a hydrogen atom. This is characteristic of a carboxylic acid functional group, COOH.\n\n- **Structure C**: This structure contains a nitrogen (N) atom bonded to two hydrogen (H) atoms and one R group, characteristic of an amine group, R-NH-R.\n\nEach structure corresponds to:\n\n- A: A-OH (Alcohol)\n- B: COOH (Carboxylic acid)\n- C: R-NH-R (Amine)\n\nMatching with the given options, the correct choice is:\n\nANSWER: A"
