"To find how many neutrons were released, we first need to balance the total mass number (A) and the atomic number (Z).\n\n1. **Add the mass numbers (A) of the reactants:**\n   \\[\n   209 (Bi) + 58 (Fe) = 267\n   \\]\n\n2. **Add the atomic numbers (Z) of the reactants:**\n   \\[\n   83 (Bi) + 26 (Fe) = 109\n   \\]\n\n3. **Subtract the mass number of Meitnerium (266) from the total mass number of the reactants (267) to find the number of neutrons released:**\n   \\[\n   267 - 266 = 1\n   \\]\n\nThe atomic numbers already balance, confirming that 1 neutron is released.\n\nANSWER: D. 1."
