"To solve this, we need to determine the DNA sequence that corresponds to the given mRNA, which is transcribed and then translated into amino acids. We need to fill in the blanks for the DNA template strand.\n\n1. From the given mRNA strand: 5'-CGU UGG UGA-3', we will determine the corresponding DNA template strand (3'-5').\n\n2. The mRNA codons translate into:\n   - CGU: Arginine (Arg)\n   - UGG: Tryptophan (Trp)\n   - UGA: Stop codon\n\n3. Using base pairing rules:\n   - DNA template strand is complementary to the mRNA:\n     - mRNA C pairs with DNA G\n     - mRNA G pairs with DNA C\n     - mRNA U pairs with DNA A\n     - mRNA A pairs with DNA T\n\n4. Apply these to the mRNA sequence:\n   - mRNA 5'-CGU-3' corresponds to DNA 3'-GCA-5'\n   - mRNA 5'-UGG-3' corresponds to DNA 3'-ACC-5'\n   - mRNA 5'-UGA-3' corresponds to DNA 3'-ACT-5'\n\n5. Fill in the DNA sequence:\n   - The complete DNA strand should be 3'-ATATTACTTTGCAACCACT-5'\n\n6. Reverse to 5'-3' orientation:\n   - 5'-ATATTACTTTGCAACCACT-3'\n\nNow match this with the given options:\n- Option A: 5'-ATATTACTTTCCATGGACT-3'\n- Option B: 5'-ATATTACTTTGCATCGACT-3'\n- Option C: 5'-ATATTACTTTGCATGCACT-3'\n- Option D: 5'-ATATTACTTTGCATGGACT-3'\n\nThe correct sequence is 5'-ATATTACTTTGCATGGACT-3', matching option D.\n\nANSWER: D"
