"To calculate Youden's index, we need to first determine the sensitivity and specificity of the electronic colposcopy method.\n\n**Sensitivity** is the probability of a positive test result given the presence of disease and is calculated as:\n\n\\[ \\text{Sensitivity} = \\frac{\\text{True Positives}}{\\text{True Positives} + \\text{False Negatives}} \\]\n\nFrom the table:\n- True Positives (TP) for electronic colposcopy: \\( 15 + 70 = 85 \\)\n- False Negatives (FN) for electronic colposcopy: \\( 5 + 10 = 15 \\)\n\n\\[ \\text{Sensitivity} = \\frac{85}{85 + 15} = \\frac{85}{100} = 0.85 \\]\n\n**Specificity** is the probability of a negative test result given the absence of disease and is calculated as:\n\n\\[ \\text{Specificity} = \\frac{\\text{True Negatives}}{\\text{True Negatives} + \\text{False Positives}} \\]\n\nFrom the table:\n- True Negatives (TN) for electronic colposcopy: \\( 220 + 245 = 465 \\)\n- False Positives (FP) for electronic colposcopy: \\( 10 + 25 = 35 \\)\n\n\\[ \\text{Specificity} = \\frac{465}{465 + 35} = \\frac{465}{500} = 0.93 \\]\n\n**Youden's Index** is calculated as:\n\n\\[ \\text{Youden's Index} = \\text{Sensitivity} + \\text{Specificity} - 1 \\]\n\nPlug in the values:\n\n\\[ \\text{Youden's Index} = 0.85 + 0.93 - 1 = 0.78 \\]\n\nANSWER: D."
"To calculate the Odds Ratio (OR) for the age group 35-39, we will use the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{OR} = \\frac{(A/C)}{(B/D)}\n\\]\n\nWhere:\n- \\( A \\) is the number of MI patients exposed to OC.\n- \\( B \\) is the number of MI patients not exposed to OC.\n- \\( C \\) is the number of control patients exposed to OC.\n- \\( D \\) is the number of control patients not exposed to OC.\n\nFrom the table for the 35-39 age group:\n- \\( A = 4 \\) (MI with OC)\n- Total MI in this age group = 37\n- Therefore, \\( B = 37 - 4 = 33 \\) (MI without OC)\n- \\( C = 26 \\) (Control with OC)\n- Total controls in this age group = 356\n- Therefore, \\( D = 356 - 26 = 330 \\) (Control without OC)\n\nNow, plug these numbers into the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{OR} = \\frac{(4/33)}{(26/330)} = \\frac{4 \\times 330}{33 \\times 26} = \\frac{1320}{858} \\approx 1.54\n\\]\n\nANSWER: C"
"To calculate the direct Benefit-Cost Ratio (BCR) in the high endemic area, use the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{Direct BCR} = \\frac{\\text{Direct benefits}}{\\text{Total cost}} \\]\n\nGiven values for the high endemic area:\n- Total cost of vaccination = 18 (RMB 10,000)\n- Direct benefits = 286 (RMB 10,000)\n\nSubstituting these values:\n\n\\[ \\text{Direct BCR} = \\frac{286}{18} \\approx 15.89 \\]\n\nThus, the direct BCR for the high endemic area is approximately 15.89.\n\nANSWER: A"
"To compute the specificity, we need to use the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Specificity} = \\frac{\\text{True Negatives (TN)}}{\\text{True Negatives (TN) + False Positives (FP)}}\n\\]\n\nFrom the table:\n- True Negatives (TN): 34 (non-patients who tested negative)\n- False Positives (FP): 33 (non-patients who tested positive)\n\nPlugging these values into the formula gives:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Specificity} = \\frac{34}{34 + 33} = \\frac{34}{67} \\approx 0.51\n\\]\n\nANSWER: B. 0.51"
"To calculate Youden's index, use the formula:\n\n**Youden's Index = Sensitivity + Specificity - 1**\n\n**Sensitivity** is the true positive rate:\n\n\\[ \\text{Sensitivity} = \\frac{\\text{True Positives}}{\\text{True Positives + False Negatives}} = \\frac{117}{125} = 0.936 \\]\n\n**Specificity** is the true negative rate:\n\n\\[ \\text{Specificity} = \\frac{\\text{True Negatives}}{\\text{True Negatives + False Positives}} = \\frac{312}{365} = 0.854 \\]\n\nNow, calculate Youden's index:\n\n\\[ \\text{Youden's Index} = 0.936 + 0.854 - 1 = 0.79 \\]\n\nANSWER: B. 0.79"
"To calculate the population attributable risk percentage (PAR%) for smoking, we use the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{PAR\\%} = \\left( \\frac{(\\text{RR} - 1) \\times \\text{Pe}}{1 + (\\text{RR} - 1) \\times \\text{Pe}} \\right) \\times 100 \\]\n\nFor smoking:\n- RR = 1.9\n- Pe = 0.72\n\nSubstitute these values into the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{PAR\\%} = \\left( \\frac{(1.9 - 1) \\times 0.72}{1 + (1.9 - 1) \\times 0.72} \\right) \\times 100 \\]\n\n\\[ \\text{PAR\\%} = \\left( \\frac{0.9 \\times 0.72}{1 + 0.9 \\times 0.72} \\right) \\times 100 \\]\n\n\\[ \\text{PAR\\%} = \\left( \\frac{0.648}{1 + 0.648} \\right) \\times 100 \\]\n\n\\[ \\text{PAR\\%} = \\left( \\frac{0.648}{1.648} \\right) \\times 100 \\]\n\n\\[ \\text{PAR\\%} = 0.393 \\times 100 \\]\n\n\\[ \\text{PAR\\%} = 39.3 \\]\n\nANSWER: C. 39.3."
