"To calculate the predicted birth weight of a baby born at 40 weeks gestational age, we can use the linear regression equation:\n\n\\[ \\text{Predicted Birth Weight} = (\\text{Beta Coefficient for Gestational Age} \\times \\text{Gestational Age}) + \\text{Constant} \\]\n\nFrom the table, we have:\n- Beta Coefficient for Gestational Age = 96.56\n- Constant = -230.34\n\nPlug in the gestational age of 40 weeks:\n\n\\[ \\text{Predicted Birth Weight} = (96.56 \\times 40) + (-230.34) \\]\n\n\\[ \\text{Predicted Birth Weight} = 3862.4 - 230.34 \\]\n\n\\[ \\text{Predicted Birth Weight} \\approx 3632.06 \\]\n\nRounding to the nearest whole number gives us 3632 grams.\n\nANSWER: A"
