"To calculate the overall Chi-square value, we must first understand how the Chi-square test works in context. The Chi-square test is used to determine if there is a significant association between categorical variables. Here, we are dealing with serum cholesterol levels (categorical) and the development of coronary heart disease (disease presence).\n\n**Step-by-step:**\n\n1. **Observed Frequencies (O):** These are given in the table as the number of cases in each cholesterol group.\n\n2. **Expected Frequencies (E):** These are calculated assuming no association between cholesterol level and disease (i.e., the probability of disease is the same across all groups).\n\n   - Total number of cases: 85\n   - Total observations: 1045\n   - Baseline probability of disease: \\( \\frac{85}{1045} \\)\n\n   For each cholesterol group:\n   \\[\n   E = \\left( \\text{number of observations in group} \\right) \\times \\left( \\text{baseline probability of disease} \\right)\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Calculate Expected Frequencies:**\n\n   - For each group: \\( E = 209 \\times \\frac{85}{1045} \\approx 17.01 \\)\n\n4. **Chi-square Calculation:**\n\n   The Chi-square statistic is computed as:\n   \\[\n   \\chi^2 = \\sum \\frac{(O - E)^2}{E}\n   \\]\n   Where \\( O \\) is the observed number of cases and \\( E \\) is the expected number of cases.\n\n   Plugging in the values:\n\n   - (114~193 mg/dl): \\( (2 - 17.01)^2 / 17.01 \\)\n   - (194~213 mg/dl): \\( (11 - 17.01)^2 / 17.01 \\)\n   - (214~230 mg/dl): \\( (14 - 17.01)^2 / 17.01 \\)\n   - (231~255 mg/dl): \\( (26 - 17.01)^2 / 17.01 \\)\n   - (256~ mg/dl): \\( (32 - 17.01)^2 / 17.01 \\)\n\n   Calculate each term, sum them to get the Chi-square statistic.\n\n5. **Calculate each component:**\n\n   - (114~193 mg/dl): \\( (2 - 17.01) = -15.01 \\); chi-square contribution = \\( \\frac{(-15.01)^2}{17.01} \\approx 13.25 \\)\n   - (194~213 mg/dl): \\( (11 - 17.01) = -6.01 \\); chi-square contribution = \\( \\frac{(-6.01)^2}{17.01} \\approx 2.12 \\)\n   - (214~230 mg/dl): \\( (14 - 17.01) = -3.01 \\); chi-square contribution = \\( \\frac{(-3.01)^2}{17.01} \\approx 0.53 \\)\n   - (231~255 mg/dl): \\( (26 - 17.01) = 8.99 \\); chi-square contribution = \\( \\frac{(8.99)^2}{17.01} \\approx 4.75 \\)\n   - (256~ mg/dl): \\( (32 - 17.01) = 14.99 \\); chi-square contribution = \\( \\frac{(14.99)^2}{17.01} \\approx 13.23 \\)\n\n6. **Sum the contributions:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\chi^2 \\approx 13.25 + 2.12 + 0.53 + 4.75 + 13.23 = 33.88\n   \\]\n\nThe closest option is:\n\nANSWER: D. 36.88"
