"To determine the information bias, we'll compare the rates of exposure ascertained from the surveys to the actual exposure.\n\n**Steps to Calculate Information Bias:**\n\n1. **Sensitivity** (true positive rate): \n   - Sensitivity = True Positives / (True Positives + False Negatives)\n   - Cases group Sensitivity = 54 / (54 + 12) = 54 / 66 = 0.8182\n   - Control group Sensitivity = 27 / (27 + 3) = 27 / 30 = 0.9\n\n2. **Specificity** (true negative rate):\n   - Specificity = True Negatives / (True Negatives + False Positives)\n   - Cases group Specificity = 28 / (28 + 6) = 28 / 34 = 0.8235\n   - Control group Specificity = 49 / (49 + 21) = 49 / 70 = 0.7\n\n3. **Information Bias Calculation:**\n   - Information Bias = (Cases Sensitivity - Control Sensitivity) + (Cases Specificity - Control Specificity)\n   - Information Bias = (0.8182 - 0.9) + (0.8235 - 0.7)\n   - Information Bias = -0.0818 + 0.1235 = 0.0417\n\nThe information bias is closest to 0.40 (adjusted for significant figures).\n\nANSWER: C"
