"To calculate the attributable risk percent (AR%) for the case of smoking and lung cancer, we use the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{AR\\%} = \\left( \\frac{\\text{Incidence in Exposed Group} - \\text{Incidence in Non-Exposed Group}}{\\text{Incidence in Exposed Group}} \\right) \\times 100 \\]\n\nGiven:\n- Incidence in the exposed group = 58\n- Incidence in the non-exposed group = 5\n\nSubstitute the values into the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{AR\\%} = \\left( \\frac{58 - 5}{58} \\right) \\times 100 \\]\n\n\\[ \\text{AR\\%} = \\left( \\frac{53}{58} \\right) \\times 100 \\]\n\n\\[ \\text{AR\\%} \\approx 91.38 \\]\n\nThe closest choice to 91.38 is option D, 0.91, indicating a probable typo or misplacement of a decimal point in the options.\n\nANSWER: D"
