"To find the relative risk (RR) of cardiovascular death for those who \"once a month\" consume fruit compared to those who consume fruit \"every day,\" we can use the following formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{RR} = \\left( \\frac{\\text{Risk in exposed group}}{\\text{Risk in control group}} \\right) \\]\n\nWhere:\n- *Risk in exposed group (once a month)* is the number of deaths divided by the number of observers in that group.\n- *Risk in control group (every day)* is the number of deaths divided by the number of observers in that group.\n\n**Calculation steps:**\n\n1. **Exposed group (once a month):**\n   - Number of deaths: 2341\n   - Number of observers: 156,098\n   - Risk = \\( \\frac{2341}{156098} \\)\n\n2. **Control group (every day):**\n   - Number of deaths: 452\n   - Number of observers: 81,386\n   - Risk = \\( \\frac{452}{81386} \\)\n\n3. **Relative Risk (RR):**\n   - RR = \\( \\frac{\\frac{2341}{156098}}{\\frac{452}{81386}} \\)\n\n4. **Calculating:**\n   - RR \u2248 \\( \\frac{0.014995}{0.005558} \\approx 2.70 \\)\n\nThe closest option to 2.70 is B. 2.68.\n\nANSWER: B. 2.68."
"To find the attributable risk (AR) of the serum cholesterol level 256 and above mg/dl group, we can use the formula for AR:\n\n\\[\nAR = \\text{Incidence in exposed group} - \\text{Incidence in reference group}\n\\]\n\n1. **Calculate the incidence in the exposed group (256 and above mg/dl):**\n\n   - Number of cases in the 256 and above mg/dl group = 32\n   - Number of observations in the 256 and above mg/dl group = 209\n\n   \\[\n   \\text{Incidence in exposed group} = \\frac{32}{209}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the incidence in the reference group (114-193 mg/dl):**\n\n   - Number of cases in the 114-193 mg/dl group = 2\n   - Number of observations in the 114-193 mg/dl group = 209\n\n   \\[\n   \\text{Incidence in reference group} = \\frac{2}{209}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Substitute the values to find AR:**\n\n   \\[\n   AR = \\frac{32}{209} - \\frac{2}{209} = \\frac{30}{209}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate AR:**\n\n   \\[\n   AR \\approx \\frac{30}{209} \\approx 0.1435 \\times 100 = 14.35\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the AR for the serum cholesterol level 256 and above mg/dl group is 14.35.\n\nANSWER: D. 14.35."
