"To find the incidence of syphilis, we need to calculate the number of cases per 100,000 people.\n\n1. **Number of syphilis cases**: 419,091\n2. **Total population in mid-2014**: 1,367,820,000\n\n\\[\n\\text{Incidence per 100,000} = \\left( \\frac{\\text{Number of syphilis cases}}{\\text{Total population}} \\right) \\times 100,000 \n\\]\n\n\\[\n= \\left( \\frac{419,091}{1,367,820,000} \\right) \\times 100,000 \n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\approx 30.64\n\\]\n\nThe incidence of syphilis is approximately 30.64 cases per 100,000 people.\n\nANSWER: A. 30.64/100,000."
