"To calculate the attributable risk percentage (AR%) for the serum cholesterol level 231-255 mg/dl group, using 114-193 mg/dl as the reference group, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the incidence rate in each group**:\n   - Reference group (114-193 mg/dl): \n     \\[\n     \\text{Incidence Rate}_\\text{Reference} = \\frac{2}{209} \n     \\]\n   - Group 231-255 mg/dl: \n     \\[\n     \\text{Incidence Rate}_\\text{231-255} = \\frac{26}{209} \n     \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the attributable risk (AR)**:\n   \\[\n   \\text{AR} = \\text{Incidence Rate}_\\text{231-255} - \\text{Incidence Rate}_\\text{Reference}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the attributable risk percentage (AR%)**:\n   \\[\n   \\text{AR\\%} = \\left(\\frac{\\text{AR}}{\\text{Incidence Rate}_\\text{231-255}}\\right) \\times 100 \n   \\]\n\nLet's compute these values:\n\n1. **Incidence rates**:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Incidence Rate}_\\text{Reference} = \\frac{2}{209} \\approx 0.00957 \n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{Incidence Rate}_\\text{231-255} = \\frac{26}{209} \\approx 0.1244 \n   \\]\n\n2. **Attributable risk (AR)**:\n   \\[\n   \\text{AR} = 0.1244 - 0.00957 = 0.11483 \n   \\]\n\n3. **Attributable risk percentage (AR%)**:\n   \\[\n   \\text{AR\\%} = \\left(\\frac{0.11483}{0.1244}\\right) \\times 100 \\approx 92.28 \n   \\]\n\nHence, the AR% of the serum cholesterol level 231-255 mg/dl group is approximately 92.28.\n\nANSWER: C"
