"To calculate the protective rate of the vaccine, we use the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Protective Rate} = \\left( \\frac{\\text{Attack rate in control group} - \\text{Attack rate in vaccination group}}{\\text{Attack rate in control group}} \\right) \\times 100\\%\n\\]\n\nFirst, we calculate the attack rates:\n\n- Attack rate in the vaccination group = \\(\\frac{50}{5000} = 0.01\\)\n- Attack rate in the control group = \\(\\frac{500}{5000} = 0.10\\)\n\nThen, apply these to the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Protective Rate} = \\left( \\frac{0.10 - 0.01}{0.10} \\right) \\times 100\\% = 0.90 \\times 100\\% = 90\\%\n\\]\n\nANSWER: D."
