"To calculate the odds ratio (OR) for lip cancer in outdoor work compared with indoor work, we use the formula for odds ratio:\n\n\\[\n\\text{OR} = \\frac{(a/c)}{(b/d)}\n\\]\n\nWhere:\n- \\( a \\) = number of lip cancer patients with outdoor work\n- \\( b \\) = number of control skin cancer patients with outdoor work\n- \\( c \\) = number of lip cancer patients with indoor work\n- \\( d \\) = number of control skin cancer patients with indoor work\n\nFrom the table:\n- \\( a = 77 + 23 = 100 \\) (lip cancer patients with outdoor work)\n- \\( b = 27 + 36 = 63 \\) (skin cancer patients with outdoor work)\n- \\( c = 36 + 5 = 41 \\)  (lip cancer patients with indoor work)\n- \\( d = 45 + 24 = 69 \\)  (skin cancer patients with indoor work)\n\nPlug these values into the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{OR} = \\frac{(100/41)}{(63/69)}\n\\]\n\nCalculate each part:\n\\[\n\\frac{100}{41} \\approx 2.44\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\frac{63}{69} \\approx 0.91\n\\]\n\nSo the OR becomes:\n\\[\n\\text{OR} = \\frac{2.44}{0.91} \\approx 2.68\n\\]\n\nComparing to the options given: \n\nA. 2.67\nB. 3.36\nC. 8.65\nD. 13.69\n\nThe closest option is A. 2.67.\n\nANSWER: A."
"To calculate the false positive rate, we follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the false positives**: These are the individuals who tested positive but do not have the disease. From the table, this number is 53.\n\n2. **Identify the true negatives**: These are the individuals who tested negative and do not have the disease. From the table, this number is 312.\n\n3. **Find the total number of people who do not have the disease**: This is the sum of false positives and true negatives. From the table:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total without disease} = 53 (\\text{false positives}) + 312 (\\text{true negatives}) = 365\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the false positive rate**: This rate is the proportion of people without the disease who tested positive.\n   \\[\n   \\text{False positive rate} = \\frac{\\text{False positives}}{\\text{Total without disease}} = \\frac{53}{365}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Compute the rate**:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{53}{365} \\approx 0.145\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the false positive rate is approximately 0.145.\n\nANSWER: C. 0.145."
