"To calculate the positive likelihood ratio (+LR), we use the formula:\n\n\\[ \n+LR = \\frac{\\text{Sensitivity}}{1 - \\text{Specificity}} \n\\]\n\nWhen the MCH cut-off is 35 pg:\n- Sensitivity = 50%\n- Specificity = 95%\n\nConvert these percentages to decimals:\n- Sensitivity = 0.50\n- Specificity = 0.95\n\nNow plug these into the formula:\n\n\\[ \n+LR = \\frac{0.50}{1 - 0.95} = \\frac{0.50}{0.05} = 10 \n\\]\n\nANSWER: C"
