"To calculate the relative risk (RR) of developing gastritis from herring consumption, we use the following formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{RR} = \\frac{\\text{Incidence rate among exposed}}{\\text{Incidence rate among unexposed}} \\]\n\nWhere:\n- Incidence rate among exposed (who ate herring) = \\(\\frac{\\text{Number of sick from herring consumption}}{\\text{Total number who ate herring}}\\)\n- Incidence rate among unexposed (who did not eat herring) = \\(\\frac{\\text{Number of sick who did not eat herring}}{\\text{Total number who did not eat herring}}\\)\n\nFrom the data:\n- Number of sick who ate herring = 200\n- Total number who ate herring = 200 (sick) + 800 (well) = 1000\n- Number of sick who did not eat herring = 100\n- Total number who did not eat herring = 100 (sick) + 900 (well) = 1000\n\nCalculating the incidence rates:\n- Incidence rate among exposed = \\(\\frac{200}{1000} = 0.2\\)\n- Incidence rate among unexposed = \\(\\frac{100}{1000} = 0.1\\)\n\nNow calculate the relative risk:\n\\[ \\text{RR} = \\frac{0.2}{0.1} = 2.0 \\]\n\nANSWER: B. 2,0."
