"To find which option describes a \"social construct,\" we need to compare each option to the provided definition.\n\nThe definition states: \"A social construct is a concept or category that has socially and culturally mediated meaning. They are concepts that generate their meaning through social and cultural worldviews.\"\n\nLet's analyze each option:\n\nA. A situation that has been constructed socially.  \n- This aligns with the idea of socially mediated meaning but isn't about a concept or category specifically.\n\nB. When an individual is shaped both mentally and physically by processors in society.  \n- This describes social influences on an individual, not the creation of social concepts.\n\nC. When society as a whole can be shaped to how it wants to be seen. It is the same over time, between societies and within societies.  \n- This implies uniformity in how societies see themselves, differing from the idea of concepts changing based on worldviews.\n\nD. When an individual creates how he or she thinks, with no influence from the outside world.  \n- This is the opposite of a social construct, which is influenced by social factors.\n\nThe best choice based on the definition provided is:\n\nANSWER: A"
