"To solve this, let's first consider what \"Majoritarianism\" refers to. Majoritarianism is a traditional political philosophy or agenda that asserts that a majority, generally categorized by religion, language, social class, or another aspect of group identity, should have the authority to make decisions that affect the society.\n\nGiven this definition, let's analyze the options:\n- A. Only the oldest group should possess the right to decide the outcome of a decision. (This is unrelated to majority rule.)\n- B. All people should possess the right to decide the outcome of a decision. (This option implies inclusiveness rather than majority rule.)\n- C. The numerical minority of a population should possess the right to decide the outcome of a decision. (This contradicts majoritarianism, which focuses on majority rule.)\n- D. The numerical majority of a population should possess the right to decide the outcome of a decision. (This aligns directly with the principle of majoritarianism.)\n\nBased on the definition and analysis, the appropriate choice is:\n\nANSWER: D."
